 .. Check that `+routineTypeDefIR'+` has type `+polyRoutineTypeDefIR+`
 .. Let `+routineTypeIR_b < tid_b* , tid_hidden_b* >+` be `+routineTypeDefIR'+`
 .. Group poly: `+routineTypeIR_a < tid_a* , tid_hidden_a* >+` and `+routineTypeIR_b < tid_b* , tid_hidden_b* >+`

  ... Check that the length of `+tid_a+`* is equal to the length of `+tid_b+`*
  ... Check that the length of `+tid_hidden_a+`* is equal to the length of `+tid_hidden_b+`*
  ... Let `+tid_fresh*+` be `+$fresh_tids(the length of tid_a* + the length of tid_hidden_a*)+`
  ... Let `+tid_a'*+` be `+tid_a* ++ tid_hidden_a*+`
  ... Let `+theta_a+` be `+{ tid_a' : TID tid_fresh* }+`
  ... Let `+routineTypeIR_a_subst+` be `+$subst_routineType(theta_a, routineTypeIR_a)+`
  ... Let `+tid_b'*+` be `+tid_b* ++ tid_hidden_b*+`
  ... Let `+theta_b+` be `+{ tid_b' : TID tid_fresh* }+`
  ... Let `+routineTypeIR_b_subst+` be `+$subst_routineType(theta_b, routineTypeIR_b)+`
  ... If [`+routineTypeIR_a_subst+` and `+routineTypeIR_b_subst+` are the same type](RoutineType_alpha), then
   .... The relation holds

