. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+ternaryExpression+`
 .. Let `+expression_cond ? expression_true : expression_false+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group ternaryExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expression_cond ? expression_true : expression_false+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_cond+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_cond+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR ctk_cond )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_cond+`
  ... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+primitiveTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+primitiveTypeIR+` be `+typeIR+`
  ... Check that `+primitiveTypeIR+` matches pattern `+BOOL+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_true+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_true+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_false+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_false+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_true, typedExpressionIR_false)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_true_cast and typedExpressionIR_false_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_cast+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_true_cast+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_true_cast+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_true_cast+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_false_cast+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_false_cast+`>>
  ... Check that `+$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR_cast) => ctk_cond =/= DYN+`
  ... Let `+ctk+` be `+$joins_ctk([ctk_cond, ctk_true_cast, and ctk_false_cast])+`
  ... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_cast ctk )+`
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_cond ? typedExpressionIR_true_cast : typedExpressionIR_false_cast # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+castExpression+`
 .. Let `+( type_t ) expression+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group castExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+( type_t ) expression+`

  ... Let `+typeIR_t+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type_t+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... If [`+typeIR_t+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p, TC)+`](Type_wf), then
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR+` can be explicitly cast to `+typeIR_t+`](Sub_expl), then
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_t ctk )+`
    ..... Result in `+( typeIR_t ) typedExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+dataExpression+`
 .. Let `+dataExpression+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. If `+dataExpression+` matches pattern `+{#}+`
  ... Group dataExpression-invalid: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+{#}+`

   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( HEADER_INVALID LCTK )+`
   .... Result in `+{#} # expressionNoteIR+`

 .. Else if `+dataExpression+` matches pattern `+{ %  % }+`
  ... Let `+{ dataElementExpression _ }+` be `+dataExpression+`
  ... If `+dataElementExpression+` has type `+expressionList+`
   .... Let `+expressionList+` be `+dataElementExpression+`
   .... Group dataExpression-sequence: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+{ expressionList _ }+`

    ..... Let `+expression_e*+` be `+$flatten_expressionList(expressionList)+`
    ..... If false
     ...... Check that `+expression_e+`* is equal to `+$flatten_expressionList(expressionList)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_e*+` be the list of `+typedExpressionIR_e+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typedExpressionIR_e+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_e+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... for each `+expression_e+` in `+expression_e*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR_e*+` be the list of `+typeIR_e+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typeIR_e+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_e+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_e+` in `+typedExpressionIR_e*+`
     ...... Let `+ctk_e*+` be the list of `+ctk_e+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+ctk_e+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_e+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_e+` in `+typedExpressionIR_e*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+SEQ < typeIR_e* >+`
     ...... Let `+ctk+` be `+$joins_ctk(ctk_e*)+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk )+`
     ...... Result in `+SEQ { typedExpressionIR_e* } # expressionNoteIR+`

    ..... Else if true
     ...... Let `+expression''*+` be `+$rev_<expression>(expression_e*)+`
     ...... Check that `+expression''*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
     ...... Let `+expression' :: expression_e_h_rev*+` be `+expression''+`*
     ...... Check that `+expression'+` has type `+defaultExpression+`
     ...... Let `+defaultExpression+` be `+expression'+`
     ...... Let `+expression_e_h*+` be `+$rev_<expression>(expression_e_h_rev*)+`
     ...... Check that ~`+...+` is in `+expression_e_h+`*
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_e_h*+` be the list of `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_e_h+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... for each `+expression_e_h+` in `+expression_e_h*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR_e_h*+` be the list of `+typeIR_e_h+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typeIR_e_h+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+` in `+typedExpressionIR_e_h*+`
     ...... Let `+ctk_e_h*+` be the list of `+ctk_e_h+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+ctk_e_h+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_e_h+` in `+typedExpressionIR_e_h*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+SEQ < typeIR_e_h* , ... >+`
     ...... Let `+ctk+` be `+$joins_ctk(ctk_e_h*)+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk )+`
     ...... Result in `+SEQ { typedExpressionIR_e_h* , ... } # expressionNoteIR+`

  ... Else if `+dataElementExpression+` has type `+recordElementExpression+`
   .... Let `+recordElementExpression+` be `+dataElementExpression+`
   .... Group dataExpression-record: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+{ recordElementExpression _ }+`

    ..... If `+recordElementExpression+` matches pattern `+% = %+`
     ...... Let `+name_f = expression_f+` be `+recordElementExpression+`
     ...... Let `+nameIR_f+` be `+$name(name_f)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_f+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_f+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... Let `+ctk_f+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+RECORD { [typeIR_f nameIR_f ;] }+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk_f )+`
     ...... Result in `+RECORD { [nameIR_f = typedExpressionIR_f] } # expressionNoteIR+`

    ..... Else if `+recordElementExpression+` matches pattern `+% = % , ...+`
     ...... Let `+name_f = expression_f , ...+` be `+recordElementExpression+`
     ...... Let `+nameIR_f+` be `+$name(name_f)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_f+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_f+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... Let `+ctk_f+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+RECORD { [typeIR_f nameIR_f ;] , ... }+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk_f )+`
     ...... Result in `+RECORD { [nameIR_f = typedExpressionIR_f] , ... } # expressionNoteIR+`

    ..... Else if `+recordElementExpression+` matches pattern `+% = % , %+`
     ...... Let `+name_f_h = expression_f_h , namedExpressionList_t+` be `+recordElementExpression+`
     ...... Let `+name_f_t = expression_f_t*+` be `+$flatten_namedExpressionList(namedExpressionList_t)+`
     ...... Let `+name_f*+` be `+name_f_h :: name_f_t*+`
     ...... Let `+nameIR_f*+` be the list of `+nameIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+nameIR_f+` be `+$name(name_f)+`
     ...... for each `+name_f+` in `+name_f*+`
     ...... Let `+expression_f*+` be `+expression_f_h :: expression_f_t*+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f*+` be the list of `+typedExpressionIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_f+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... for each `+expression_f+` in `+expression_f*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR_f*+` be the list of `+typeIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typeIR_f+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_f+` in `+typedExpressionIR_f*+`
     ...... Let `+ctk_f*+` be the list of `+ctk_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+ctk_f+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_f+` in `+typedExpressionIR_f*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+RECORD { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+`
     ...... Let `+ctk+` be `+$joins_ctk(ctk_f*)+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk )+`
     ...... Result in `+RECORD { nameIR_f = typedExpressionIR_f* } # expressionNoteIR+`

    ..... Else if `+recordElementExpression+` matches pattern `+% = % , % , ...+`
     ...... Let `+name_f_h = expression_f_h , namedExpressionList_t , ...+` be `+recordElementExpression+`
     ...... Let `+name_f_t = expression_f_t*+` be `+$flatten_namedExpressionList(namedExpressionList_t)+`
     ...... Let `+name_f*+` be `+name_f_h :: name_f_t*+`
     ...... Let `+nameIR_f*+` be the list of `+nameIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+nameIR_f+` be `+$name(name_f)+`
     ...... for each `+name_f+` in `+name_f*+`
     ...... Let `+expression_f*+` be `+expression_f_h :: expression_f_t*+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f*+` be the list of `+typedExpressionIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typedExpressionIR_f+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_f+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... for each `+expression_f+` in `+expression_f*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR_f*+` be the list of `+typeIR_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+typeIR_f+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_f+` in `+typedExpressionIR_f*+`
     ...... Let `+ctk_f*+` be the list of `+ctk_f+`, obtained by repeating:
      ....... Let `+ctk_f+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_f+`>>
     ...... for each `+typedExpressionIR_f+` in `+typedExpressionIR_f*+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR+` be `+RECORD { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* , ... }+`
     ...... Let `+ctk+` be `+$joins_ctk(ctk_f*)+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk )+`
     ...... Result in `+RECORD { nameIR_f = typedExpressionIR_f* , ... } # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+errorAccessExpression+`
 .. Let `+ERROR . member+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group errorAccessExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+ERROR . member+`

  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
  ... Let `+nameIR_error+` be `+"error." ++ nameIR+`
  ... Check that `+ERROR . nameIR+` is equal to `+$find_value(p, TC, ` nameIR_error)+`
  ... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( ERROR LCTK )+`
  ... Result in `+ERROR . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+memberAccessExpression+`
 .. Let `+memberAccessBase . member+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. If `+memberAccessBase+` has type `+prefixedTypeName+`
  ... Let `+prefixedTypeName_base+` be `+memberAccessBase+`
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-type: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+prefixedTypeName_base . member+`

   .... Let `+prefixedNameIR_base+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName_base)+`
   .... Let `+typeDefIR'?+` be `+$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR_base)+`
   .... Check that `+typeDefIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typeDefIR)+` be `+typeDefIR'+`?
   .... Check that `+typeDefIR+` has type `+typeIR+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be `+typeDefIR+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+enumTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+enumTypeIR+` be `+typeIR+`
   .... If `+enumTypeIR+` matches pattern `+ENUM % { % }+`
    ..... Let `+ENUM _ { nameIR_f* }+` be `+enumTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+nameIR_f+`*
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_base LCTK )+`
    ..... Result in `+TYPE prefixedNameIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

   .... Else if `+enumTypeIR+` matches pattern `+ENUM % # % { % }+`
    ..... Let `+ENUM _ # _ { nameIR_f = _ ;* }+` be `+enumTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+nameIR_f+`*
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_base LCTK )+`
    ..... Result in `+TYPE prefixedNameIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

 .. Else if `+memberAccessBase+` has type `+expression+`
  ... Let `+expression_base+` be `+memberAccessBase+`
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-expression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expression_base . member+`

   .... If "size" is equal to `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
    ..... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( BIT < 32 > LCTK )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "size" # expressionNoteIR+`
   .... If "lastIndex" is equal to `+$name(member)+`
    ..... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( BIT < 32 > DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "lastIndex" # expressionNoteIR+`
    ..... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( BIT < 32 > DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "lastIndex" # expressionNoteIR+`
   .... If "last" is equal to `+$name(member)+`
    ..... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "last" # expressionNoteIR+`
    ..... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "last" # expressionNoteIR+`
   .... If "next" is equal to `+$name(member)+`
    ..... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "next" # expressionNoteIR+`
    ..... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
     ...... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
     ...... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
     ...... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . "next" # expressionNoteIR+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... If `+typeIR'+` has type `+structTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+STRUCT _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

   .... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+HEADER _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

   .... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerUnionTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

   .... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+tableTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+tableTypeIR+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Check that `+tableTypeIR+` matches pattern `+TABLE_STRUCT % { % }+`
    ..... Let `+TABLE_STRUCT _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+tableTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+indexAccessExpression+`
 .. Let `+expression_base [ expression_index ]+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group indexAccessExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expression_base [ expression_index ]+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_index+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_index+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_base+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_index+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_index+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_index+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_index+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_index, $compat_array_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_index_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
  ... If `+typeIR'+` has type `+tupleTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+TUPLE < typeIR_e* >+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... Check that `+ctk_index+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
   .... Let `+value_index+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_index_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value_index)+`
   .... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
   .... Let `+n_index+` be `+int+`
   .... Check that `+n_index+` is less than the length of `+typeIR_e+`*
   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_e*[n_index] DYN )+`
   .... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index_reduced ] # expressionNoteIR+`

  ... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... If true
    ..... Let `+value_index+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_index_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value_index)+`
    ..... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
    ..... Let `+n_index+` be `+int+`
    ..... Check that `+n_index+` is less than `+n_size+`
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index_reduced ] # expressionNoteIR+`

   .... Else if false
    ..... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR DYN )+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index_reduced ] # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+sliceAccessExpression+`
 .. Let `+expression_base [ expression_hi : expression_lo ]+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group sliceAccessExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expression_base [ expression_hi : expression_lo ]+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_hi+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_hi+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_lo+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_lo+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_base, $compat_bitslice_base)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_base_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_base_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_base_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_base_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_hi, $compat_bitslice_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR''?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_lo, $compat_bitslice_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR''+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_hi_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_hi_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_lo_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_lo_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced+`>>
  ... Check that `+ctk_hi_reduced+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
  ... Let `+value_hi+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value_hi)+`
  ... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_hi+` be `+int+`
  ... Check that `+ctk_lo_reduced+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
  ... Let `+value_lo+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+int'+` be `+$to_number(value_lo)+`
  ... Check that `+int'+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_lo+` be `+int'+`
  ... Check that `+$is_valid_bitslice(typeIR_base_reduced, n_lo, n_hi)+`
  ... Let `+int''+` be `+n_hi - n_lo + 1+`
  ... Check that `+int''+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_slice+` be `+int''+`
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be `+BIT < n_slice >+`
  ... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk_base_reduced )+`
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced : typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced ] # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+callExpression+`
 .. Let `+callExpression+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group callExpression-routine: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+callExpression+`

  ... If `+callExpression+` matches pattern `+% ( % )+`
   .... Let `+callTarget ( argumentList )+` be `+callExpression+`
   .... Check that `+callTarget+` has type `+routineTarget+`
   .... Let `+routineTarget+` be `+callTarget+`
   .... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_ok, the result of typing `+routineTarget+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... (RoutineType_ok: `+p TC |- routineTargetIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : routineTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_inserted+`*
   .... (Call_ok: `+p TC |- routineTypeIR < [] # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_ret < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Check that `+typeIR_ret+` is not equal to `+VOID+`
   .... Let `+ctk+` be `+$is_static_routineTarget(routineTargetIR)+`
   .... Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`
   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_ret ctk )+`
   .... Result in `+callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR+`

  ... Else if `+callExpression+` matches pattern `+% < % > ( % )+`
   .... Let `+routineTarget < realTypeArgumentList > ( argumentList )+` be `+callExpression+`
   .... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_ok, the result of typing `+routineTarget+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+realTypeArgument*+` be `+$flatten_realTypeArgumentList(realTypeArgumentList)+`
   .... (TypeArguments_ok: `+p TC |- realTypeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid_impl*+`)
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... (RoutineType_ok: `+p TC |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : routineTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_impl* ++ tid_inserted*+`
   .... (Call_ok: `+p TC |- routineTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_ret < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Check that `+typeIR_ret+` is not equal to `+VOID+`
   .... Let `+ctk+` be `+$is_static_routineTarget(routineTargetIR)+`
   .... Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`
   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_ret ctk )+`
   .... Result in `+callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR+`
 .. Check that `+callExpression+` matches pattern `+% ( % )+`
 .. Let `+callTarget ( argumentList )+` be `+callExpression+`
 .. Group callExpression-constructor: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+callTarget ( argumentList )+`

  ... If `+callTarget+` has type `+prefixedTypeName+`
   .... Let `+prefixedTypeName+` be `+callTarget+`
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
   .... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p TC |- prefixedNameIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_impl* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... (Inst_ok: `+p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < [] # tid_impl* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Check that `+$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR_object)+`
   .... Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`
   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_object CTK )+`
   .... Result in `+callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR+`

  ... Else if `+callTarget+` has type `+specializedType+`
   .... Let `+prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >+` be `+callTarget+`
   .... Let `+typeArgument*+` be `+$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)+`
   .... (TypeArguments_ok: `+p TC |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid_impl*+`)
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
   .... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p TC |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_impl* ++ tid_inserted*+`
   .... (Inst_ok: `+p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Check that `+$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR_object)+`
   .... Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`
   .... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR_object CTK )+`
   .... Result in `+callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR+`

. Else if `+expression'''+` has type `+parenthesizedExpression+`
 .. Let `+( expression )+` be `+expression'''+`
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+( expression )+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
  ... Let `+expressionNoteIR+` be `+( typeIR ctk )+`
  ... Result in `+( typedExpressionIR ) # expressionNoteIR+`

relation Argument_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+argument+`

. Check that `+argument+` has type `+expression+`
. Let `+expression+` be `+argument+`
. Group expression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expression+`

 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
 .. Result in `+typedExpressionIR+`
. If `+argument+` matches pattern `+% = %+`
 .. Let `+name = expression+` be `+argument+`
 .. Group name-expression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+name = expression+`

  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Result in `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR+`

. Else if `+argument+` matches pattern `+% = _+`
 .. Let `+name = _+` be `+argument+`
 .. Group name-dontcare: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+name = _+`

  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
  ... Result in `+nameIR = _+`

. Else if `+argument+` matches pattern `+_+`
 .. Group dontcare: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+_+`

  ... Result in `+_+`

relation Lvalue_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue+`

. Check that `+lvalue+` has type `+prefixedNonTypeName+`
. Let `+prefixedNonTypeName+` be `+lvalue+`
. Group referenceExpression-prefixedNonTypeName: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+prefixedNonTypeName+`

 .. Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)+`
 .. Let `+varTypeIR?+` be `+$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)+`
 .. Check that `+varTypeIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
 .. Let `+?(direction typeIR ctk value?)+` be `+varTypeIR+`?
 .. Check that `+ctk+` matches pattern `+DYN+`
 .. Check that `+value?+` matches pattern `+()+`
 .. If `+direction+` matches pattern `+OUT+`
  ... Result in `+prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )+`

 .. Else if `+direction+` matches pattern `+INOUT+`
  ... Result in `+prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )+`
. If `+lvalue+` matches pattern `+% . %+`
 .. Let `+lvalue_base . member+` be `+lvalue+`
 .. Group memberAccess: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue_base . member+`

  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR_base+` be <<Lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_base )+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base+`
  ... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
  ... If `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+typeIR [ _ ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... If `+nameIR+` = "next"
    ..... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`
    ..... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

   .... Else if `+nameIR+` = "last"
    ..... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`
    ..... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
     ...... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
     ...... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

  ... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+structTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+STRUCT _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
   .... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
   .... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

  ... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+HEADER _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
   .... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
   .... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

  ... Else if `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerUnionTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR_f nameIR_f ;* }+` be `+typeIR'+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR''?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR_f and typeIR_f)*)+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR''?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typeIR)+` be `+typeIR''+`?
   .... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base . nameIR # ( typeIR )+`
   .... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

. Else if `+lvalue+` matches pattern `+% [ % ]+`
 .. Let `+lvalue_base [ expression_index ]+` be `+lvalue+`
 .. Group indexAccess: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue_base [ expression_index ]+`

  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR_base+` be <<Lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_base )+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base+`
  ... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
  ... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+typeIR [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_index+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_index+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_index ctk_index )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_index+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_index, $compat_array_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_index_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... If true
   .... Let `+value_index+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_index_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value_index)+`
   .... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
   .... Let `+n_index+` be `+int+`
   .... Check that `+n_index+` is less than `+n_size+`
   .... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index_reduced ] # ( typeIR )+`
   .... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

  ... Else if false
   .... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index_reduced ] # ( typeIR )+`
   .... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

. Else if `+lvalue+` matches pattern `+% [ % : % ]+`
 .. Let `+lvalue_base [ expression_hi : expression_lo ]+` be `+lvalue+`
 .. Group sliceAccess: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue_base [ expression_hi : expression_lo ]+`

  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR_base+` be <<Lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_base )+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base+`
  ... Check that `+$compat_bitslice_base(typeIR_base)+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_hi+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_hi+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_lo+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_lo+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_hi, $compat_bitslice_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR_lo, $compat_bitslice_index)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_hi_reduced ctk_hi_reduced )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced+`
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_lo_reduced ctk_lo_reduced )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced+`
  ... Check that `+ctk_hi_reduced+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
  ... Let `+value_hi+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value_hi)+`
  ... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_hi+` be `+int+`
  ... Check that `+ctk_lo_reduced+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
  ... Let `+value_lo+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+int'+` be `+$to_number(value_lo)+`
  ... Check that `+int'+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_lo+` be `+int'+`
  ... Check that `+$is_valid_bitslice(typeIR_base, n_lo, n_hi)+`
  ... Let `+int''+` be `+n_hi - n_lo + 1+`
  ... Check that `+int''+` has type `+nat+`
  ... Let `+n_slice+` be `+int''+`
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be `+BIT < n_slice >+`
  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi_reduced : typedExpressionIR_lo_reduced ] # ( typeIR )+`
  ... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

. Else if `+lvalue+` matches pattern `+( % )+`
 .. Let `+( lvalue_base )+` be `+lvalue+`
 .. Group parenthesized: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+( lvalue_base )+`

  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR_base+` be <<Lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_base )+` be `+typedLvalueIR_base+`
  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be `+( typedLvalueIR_base ) # ( typeIR_base )+`
  ... Result in `+typedLvalueIR+`

relation Stmt_ok: `+p'+`, `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+statement+`

. If `+statement+` has type `+emptyStatement+`
 .. Let `+emptyStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group emptyStatement: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+;+`

  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+;+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+assignmentStatement+`
 .. Let `+lvalue assignop expression ;+` be `+statement+`
 .. Check that `+assignop+` matches pattern `+=+`
 .. Group assignmentStatement-eq: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+lvalue = expression ;+`

  ... Let `+typedLvalueIR+` be <<Lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_l+` be `+$typeof_lvalue(typedLvalueIR)+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_r+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR, typeIR_l)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+typedLvalueIR = typedExpressionIR_cast ;+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+callStatement+`
 .. Let `+callStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group callStatement: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+callStatement+`

  ... If `+callStatement+` matches pattern `+% ( % ) ;+`
   .... Let `+lvalue_routine ( argumentList ) ;+` be `+callStatement+`
   .... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_routine+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... (RoutineType_ok: `+p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : routineTypeIR < # tid_impl* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... (Call_ok: `+p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [] # tid_impl* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_ret < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Let `+callStatementIR+` be `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* ) ;+`
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+callStatementIR+`

  ... Else if `+callStatement+` matches pattern `+% < % > ( % ) ;+`
   .... Let `+lvalue_routine < typeArgumentList > ( argumentList ) ;+` be `+callStatement+`
   .... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue_routine+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... Let `+typeArgument*+` be `+$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)+`
   .... (TypeArguments_ok: `+p' TC' |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid_impl*+`)
   .... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
   .... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
   .... (RoutineType_ok: `+p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : routineTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
   .... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_impl* ++ tid_inserted*+`
   .... (Call_ok: `+p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [] # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_ret < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
   .... Let `+callStatementIR+` be `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* ) ;+`
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+callStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+directApplicationStatement+`
 .. Let `+namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group directApplicationStatement: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, `+f+`, and `+namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;+`

  ... Let `+expressionIR # ( typeIR_object _ )+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+namedType ( )+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
  ... Check that `+expressionIR+` has type `+callExpressionIR+`
  ... Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
  ... Check that `+callExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+% ( % )+`
  ... Let `+prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* )+` be `+callExpressionIR+`
  ... Check that `+typeArgumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Check that `+argumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Check that `+$compat_direct_application(typeIR_object)+`
  ... Let `+nameIR_object+` be "__direct_application"
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(p', TC', nameIR_object, typeIR_object CTK ?())+`
  ... Let `+lvalue+` be `+nameIR_object . "apply"+`
  ... Let `+_+`, `+_+`, and `+statementIR+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+lvalue ( argumentList ) ;+`, under cursor `+p'+`, typing context `+TC_1+`, and flow `+f'+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
  ... Check that `+statementIR+` has type `+callStatementIR+`
  ... Let `+callStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
  ... Let `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR'* > ( argumentIR_cast* ) ;+` be `+callStatementIR+`
  ... Check that `+routineTargetIR+` is equal to `+` nameIR_object # ( typeIR_object CTK ) . "apply"+`
  ... Check that `+typeArgumentIR'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+directApplicationStatementIR+` be `+prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentIR_cast* ) ;+`
  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+directApplicationStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+exitStatement+`
 .. Let `+exitStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group exitStatement: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+EXIT ;+`

  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+EXIT ;+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+conditionalStatement+`
 .. Let `+conditionalStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group conditionalStatement: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+conditionalStatement+`

  ... If `+conditionalStatement+` matches pattern `+IF ( % ) %+`
   .... Let `+IF ( expression_cond ) statement_then+` be `+conditionalStatement+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_cond+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_cond+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR_cond+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_cond+`>>
   .... Check that `+BOOL+` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_cond+`>>
   .... Let `+TC_then+`, `+f_then+`, and `+statementIR_then+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+statement_then+`, under cursor `+p'+`, typing context `+TC'+`, and flow `+f'+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f'+`, and `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then+`

  ... Else if `+conditionalStatement+` matches pattern `+IF ( % ) % ELSE %+`
   .... Let `+IF ( expression_cond ) statement_then ELSE statement_else+` be `+conditionalStatement+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_cond+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_cond+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR_cond+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_cond+`>>
   .... Check that `+BOOL+` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_cond+`>>
   .... Let `+TC_then+`, `+f_then+`, and `+statementIR_then+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+statement_then+`, under cursor `+p'+`, typing context `+TC'+`, and flow `+f'+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
   .... Let `+TC_else+`, `+f_else+`, and `+statementIR_else+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+statement_else+`, under cursor `+p'+`, typing context `+TC'+`, and flow `+f'+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
   .... Let `+f_post+` be <<join_flow, the merged control flow of `+f_then+` and `+f_else+`>>
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f_post+`, and `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then ELSE statementIR_else+`
. Check that `+p'+` matches pattern `+LOCAL+`
. If `+statement+` has type `+returnStatement+`
 .. Let `+returnStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group returnStatement: `+LOCAL+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+returnStatement+`

  ... If `+returnStatement+` matches pattern `+RETURN ;+`
   .... Check that ?(`+VOID+`) is equal to `+$find_return_type(TC')+`
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+RET+`, and `+RETURN ;+`

  ... Else if `+returnStatement+` matches pattern `+RETURN % ;+`
   .... Let `+RETURN expression ;+` be `+returnStatement+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR'?+` be `+$find_return_type(TC')+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typeIR_ret)+` be `+typeIR'+`?
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR, typeIR_ret)+`
   .... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
   .... Result in `+TC'+`, `+RET+`, and `+RETURN typedExpressionIR_cast ;+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+blockStatement+`
 .. Let `+blockStatement+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group blockStatement: `+LOCAL+`, `+TC_0+`, `+f_0+`, and `+blockStatement+`

  ... (Block_ok: `+TC' f' |- blockStatement : TC_1 f_1 blockStatementIR+`)
  ... Result in `+TC_1+`, `+f_1+`, and `+blockStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statement+` has type `+switchStatement+`
 .. Let `+SWITCH ( expression_switch ) { switchCaseList }+` be `+statement+`
 .. Group switchStatement-table: `+LOCAL+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+SWITCH ( expression_switch ) { switchCaseList }+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_switch+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_switch+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_switch+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_switch+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_switch+`>>
  ... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+tableTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+tableTypeIR+` be `+typeIR+`
  ... Check that `+tableTypeIR+` matches pattern `+TABLE_ENUM % { % }+`
  ... Let `+TABLE_ENUM tid_table_enum { _* }+` be `+tableTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+tid_table+` be `+$strip_prefix($strip_suffix(tid_table_enum, ")"), "action_list(")+`
  ... Let `+switchCase*+` be `+$flatten_switchCaseList(switchCaseList)+`
  ... (SwitchCases_table_ok: `+TC' f' tid_table |- switchCase* : f_post switchCaseIR* # switchLabel*+`)
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `+switchLabel*+` are distinct>>
  ... Let `+switchStatementIR+` be `+SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR_switch ) { switchCaseIR* }+`
  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f_post+`, and `+switchStatementIR+`
 .. Group switchStatement-general: `+LOCAL+`, `+TC+`, `+f+`, and `+SWITCH ( expression_switch ) { switchCaseList }+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_switch+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_switch+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC'+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR_switch+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_switch+`>>
  ... Check that `+$compat_switch(typeIR_switch)+`
  ... Let `+switchCase*+` be `+$flatten_switchCaseList(switchCaseList)+`
  ... (SwitchCases_general_ok: `+TC' f' typeIR_switch |- switchCase* : f_post switchCaseIR* # switchLabel*+`)
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `+switchLabel*+` are distinct>>
  ... Let `+switchStatementIR+` be `+SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR_switch ) { switchCaseIR* }+`
  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+f_post+`, and `+switchStatementIR+`

relation BlockElementStmt_ok: `+TC_0+`, `+f+`, and `+blockElementStatement+`

. If `+blockElementStatement+` has type `+constantDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+constantDeclaration+` be `+blockElementStatement+`
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `+TC_0+`, `+f+`, and `+constantDeclaration+`

