  ... If `+initializerOpt+` has type `+initializer+`
   .... Let `+= expression_init+` be `+initializerOpt+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
   .... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(LOCAL, TC_0)+`](Type_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_init+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_init+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_init, typeIR)+`
    ..... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_init_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(LOCAL, TC_0, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())+`
    ..... Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR nameIR ?(= typedExpressionIR_init_cast) ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+`, `+f+`, and `+variableDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+blockElementStatement+` has type `+statement+`
 .. Let `+statement+` be `+blockElementStatement+`
 .. Group statement: `+TC_0+`, `+f+`, and `+statement+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+`, `+f_post+`, and `+statementIR+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+statement+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+`, typing context `+TC_0+`, and flow `+f+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
