relation ParserTransition_ok: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `+transitionStatement+`

. If `+transitionStatement+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
 .. Group empty: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `++`

  ... Result in `+TRANSITION "reject" ;+`

. Else if `+transitionStatement+` matches pattern `+TRANSITION %+`
 .. Let `+TRANSITION stateExpression+` be `+transitionStatement+`
 .. If `+stateExpression+` matches pattern `+% ;+`
  ... Let `+name ;+` be `+stateExpression+`
  ... Group name: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `+TRANSITION name ;+`

   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
   .... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+nameIR_state+`*
   .... Let `+transitionStatementIR+` be `+TRANSITION nameIR ;+`
   .... Result in `+transitionStatementIR+`
 .. If `+stateExpression+` has type `+selectExpression+`
  ... Let `+SELECT ( expressionList_key ) { selectCaseList }+` be `+stateExpression+`
  ... Group switch: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `+TRANSITION SELECT ( expressionList_key ) { selectCaseList }+`

   .... Let `+expression_key*+` be `+$flatten_expressionList(expressionList_key)+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_key*+` be the list of `+typedExpressionIR_key+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_key+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_key+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
   .... for each `+expression_key+` in `+expression_key*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_key*+` be the list of `+typeIR_key+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+typeIR_key+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_key+`>>
   .... for each `+typedExpressionIR_key+` in `+typedExpressionIR_key*+`
   .... If [`+SET < [typeIR_key] >+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(LOCAL, TC_0)+`](Type_wf), for each `+typeIR_key+` in `+typeIR_key*+`, then
    ..... Let `+selectCase*+` be `+$flatten_selectCaseList(selectCaseList)+`
    ..... (SelectCase_ok: `+TC_0 nameIR_state* typeIR_key* |- selectCase : selectCaseIR+`), for each `+selectCase+` in `+selectCase*+` and `+selectCaseIR+` in `+selectCaseIR*+`
    ..... Let `+transitionStatementIR+` be `+TRANSITION SELECT ( typedExpressionIR_key* ) { selectCaseIR* }+`
    ..... Result in `+transitionStatementIR+`

relation ParserStmt_ok: `+TC_0'+` and `+parserStatement''+`

. If `+parserStatement''+` has type `+constantDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+constantDeclaration+` be `+parserStatement''+`
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+constantDeclaration+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+constantDeclaration+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0'+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+constantDeclarationIR+`
  ... Let `+constantDeclarationIR+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+constantDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+parserStatement''+` has type `+variableDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList type name initializerOpt ;+` be `+parserStatement''+`
 .. Group variableDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+annotationList type name initializerOpt ;+`

  ... If `+initializerOpt+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0'+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
   .... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(LOCAL, TC_0')+`](Type_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(LOCAL, TC_0', nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())+`
    ..... Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+variableDeclarationIR+`
  ... If `+initializerOpt+` has type `+initializer+`
   .... Let `+= expression_init+` be `+initializerOpt+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0'+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
   .... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(LOCAL, TC_0')+`](Type_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_init+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_init+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_0'+`>>
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_init, typeIR)+`
    ..... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_init_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(LOCAL, TC_0', nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())+`
    ..... Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR nameIR ?(= typedExpressionIR_init_cast) ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+variableDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+parserStatement''+` has type `+emptyStatement+`
 .. Let `+emptyStatement+` be `+parserStatement''+`
 .. Group emptyStatement: `+TC+` and `+emptyStatement+`

  ... Let `+typingContext+`, `+flow+`, and `+statementIR+` be <<Stmt_ok, the result of typing `+emptyStatement+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+`, typing context `+TC_0'+`, and flow `+CONT+`, with the modified typing context and flow>>
  ... Check that `+typingContext+` is equal to `+TC_0'+`
  ... Check that `+flow+` matches pattern `+CONT+`
  ... Check that `+statementIR+` has type `+emptyStatementIR+`
