relation ParserState_ok: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `+annotationList STATE name { parserStatementList transitionStatement }+`

. Group : `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, and `+annotationList STATE name { parserStatementList transitionStatement }+`

 .. Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
 .. Let `+TC_1+` be `+$enter(TC_0)+`
 .. Let `+parserStatement*+` be `+$flatten_parserStatementList(parserStatementList)+`
 .. (ParserStmts_ok: `+TC_1 |- parserStatement* : TC_2 parserStatementIR*+`)
 .. (ParserTransition_ok: `+TC_2 nameIR_state* |- transitionStatement : transitionStatementIR+`)
 .. Let `+TC_3+` be `+$exit(TC_2)+`
 .. Let `+parserStateIR+` be `+annotationList STATE nameIR { parserStatementIR* transitionStatementIR }+`
 .. Result in `+parserStateIR+`

relation ParserStates_ok: `+TC+` and `+parserState+`*

. Group : `+TC+` and `+parserState+`*

 .. Let `+_annotationList*+` be the list of `+_annotationList+`, `+_parserStatementList*+` be the list of `+_parserStatementList+`, `+_transitionStatement*+` be the list of `+_transitionStatement+`, and `+name_state*+` be the list of `+name_state+`, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let `+_ STATE name_state { _ _ }+` be `+parserState+`
 .. for each `+parserState+` in `+parserState*+`
 .. Let `+nameIR_state*+` be the list of `+nameIR_state+`, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let `+nameIR_state+` be `+$name(name_state)+`
 .. for each `+name_state+` in `+name_state*+`
 .. Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `+nameIR_state*+` are distinct>>
 .. Check that "start" is in `+nameIR_state+`*
 .. Check that `+~"accept" is in nameIR_state* /\ ~"reject" is in nameIR_state*+`
 .. Let `+nameIR_state_impl*+` be `+"accept" :: "reject" :: nameIR_state*+`
 .. (ParserState_ok: `+TC nameIR_state_impl* |- parserState : parserStateIR+`), for each `+parserState+` in `+parserState*+` and `+parserStateIR+` in `+parserStateIR*+`
 .. Result in `+parserStateIR*+`

