  ... (TableEntry_keyset_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 |- keysetExpression : TBLS keysetExpressionIR+`)
  ... (TableEntry_action_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 |- tableActionReference : tableActionReferenceIR+`)
  ... (TableEntry_priority_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 TBLS |- ?(tableEntryPriority) : TBLC_1 tableEntryPriorityOptIR+`)
  ... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tableEntryIR+` be `+constOptIR tableEntryPriorityOptIR keysetExpressionIR : tableActionReferenceIR annotationList ;+`
  ... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tableEntryIR+`

. Else if `+tableEntry+` matches pattern `+%  % : %  % ;+`
 .. Let `+constOpt keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;+` be `+tableEntry+`
 .. Group non-priority: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+constOpt keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;+`

  ... (TableEntry_keyset_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 |- keysetExpression : TBLS keysetExpressionIR+`)
  ... (TableEntry_action_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 |- tableActionReference : tableActionReferenceIR+`)
  ... (TableEntry_priority_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 TBLS |- ?() : TBLC_1 tableEntryPriorityOptIR+`)
  ... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tableEntryIR+` be `+constOptIR tableEntryPriorityOptIR keysetExpressionIR : tableActionReferenceIR annotationList ;+`
  ... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tableEntryIR+`

relation TableEntries_ok: `+TC+`, `+TBLC'+`, and `+tableEntry+`*

. If `+tableEntry*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TBLC'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+tableEntry*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+tableEntry_h :: tableEntry_t*+` be `+tableEntry+`*
 .. Group cons: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+tableEntry_h :: tableEntry_t*+`

  ... (TableEntry_ok: `+TC TBLC' |- tableEntry_h : TBLC_1 tableEntryIR_h+`)
  ... (TableEntries_ok: `+TC TBLC_1 |- tableEntry_t* : TBLC_2 tableEntryIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLC_2+` and `+tableEntryIR_h :: tableEntryIR_t*+`

relation TableProperty_ok: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0'+`, and `+tableProperty+`

. If `+tableProperty+` matches pattern `+KEY = { % }+`
 .. Let `+KEY = { tableKeyList }+` be `+tableProperty+`
 .. Group key: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+KEY = { tableKeyList }+`

  ... Let `+tableKey*+` be `+$flatten_tableKeyList(tableKeyList)+`
  ... (TableKeys_ok: `+TC TBLC_0' |- tableKey* : TBLC_1 tableKeyIR*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+KEY = { tableKeyIR* }+`

. Else if `+tableProperty+` matches pattern `+ACTIONS = { % }+`
 .. Let `+ACTIONS = { tableActionList }+` be `+tableProperty+`
 .. Group actions: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+ACTIONS = { tableActionList }+`

  ... Let `+tableAction*+` be `+$flatten_tableActionList(tableActionList)+`
  ... (TableActions_ok: `+TC TBLC_0' |- tableAction* : TBLC_1 tableActionIR*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+ACTIONS = { tableActionIR* }+`

. Else if `+tableProperty+` matches pattern `+%  % ENTRIES = { % }+`
 .. Let `+annotationList constOpt ENTRIES = { tableEntryList }+` be `+tableProperty+`
 .. Group entries: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+annotationList constOpt ENTRIES = { tableEntryList }+`

  ... Let `+tableEntry*+` be `+$flatten_tableEntryList(tableEntryList)+`
  ... Check that `+the length of TBLC_0'.KEYS = 0 => the length of tableEntry* = 0+`
  ... Let `+TBLC_1+` be `+TBLC_0'+`[ENTRIES.SIZE = the length of `+tableEntry+`*]
  ... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
  ... Let `+TBLC_2+` be `+TBLC_1+`[ENTRIES.CONST = `+constOptIR+` is equal to ?(`+CONST+`)]
  ... (TableEntries_ok: `+TC TBLC_2 |- tableEntry* : TBLC_3 tableEntryIR*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLC_3+` and `+annotationList constOptIR ENTRIES = { tableEntryIR* }+`

. Else if `+tableProperty+` matches pattern `+%  %  %  % ;+`
 .. Let `+annotationList constOpt tableCustomName initializer ;+` be `+tableProperty+`
 .. Group default-action: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, and `+annotationList constOpt tableCustomName initializer ;+`

  ... Check that "default_action" is equal to `+$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)+`
  ... (TableDefaultAction_ok: `+TC TBLC_0' |- initializer : tableActionReferenceIR+`)
  ... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR DEFAULT_ACTION = tableActionReferenceIR ;+`
  ... Result in `+TBLC_0'+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
 .. Let `+annotationList constOpt tableCustomName = expression ;+` be `+tableProperty+`
 .. Group custom: `+TC+`, `+tableContext+`, and `+annotationList constOpt tableCustomName = expression ;+`

  ... If "size" is equal to `+$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... If `+$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_0'+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
   .... If `+$is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_0'+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
   .... If `+$is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_0'+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
  ... If "largest_priority_wins" is equal to `+$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... Check that `+BOOL+` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR+`>>
   .... Let `+value'+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Check that `+value'+` has type `+primitiveValue+`
   .... Let `+primitiveValue+` be `+value'+`
   .... Check that `+primitiveValue+` matches pattern `+B %+`
   .... Let `+B b_largest_priority_wins+` be `+primitiveValue+`
   .... Let `+TBLC_1+` be `+TBLC_0'+`[PRIORITIES.LARGEST_WINS = `+b_largest_priority_wins+`]
   .... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
   .... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "largest_priority_wins" = B b_largest_priority_wins ;+`
   .... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
  ... If "priority_delta" is equal to `+$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... If `+$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+value+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value)+`
    ..... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
    ..... Let `+n_delta+` be `+int+`
    ..... Check that `+n_delta+` is greater than 0
    ..... Let `+TBLC_1+` be `+TBLC_0'+`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `+n_delta+`]
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n_delta ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
   .... If `+$is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+value+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value)+`
    ..... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
    ..... Let `+n_delta+` be `+int+`
    ..... Check that `+n_delta+` is greater than 0
    ..... Let `+TBLC_1+` be `+TBLC_0'+`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `+n_delta+`]
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n_delta ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
   .... If `+$is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+value+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+int+` be `+$to_number(value)+`
    ..... Check that `+int+` has type `+nat+`
    ..... Let `+n_delta+` be `+int+`
    ..... Check that `+n_delta+` is greater than 0
    ..... Let `+TBLC_1+` be `+TBLC_0'+`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `+n_delta+`]
    ..... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
    ..... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n_delta ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`
  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)+`
  ... If `+nameIR =/= "size" /\ nameIR =/= "largest_priority_wins" /\ nameIR =/= "priority_delta"+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+constOptIR+` be `+$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)+`
   .... Let `+tablePropertyIR+` be `+annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM nameIR = typedExpressionIR ;+`
   .... Result in `+TBLC_0'+` and `+tablePropertyIR+`

relation TableProperties_ok: `+TC+`, `+TBLC'+`, and `+tableProperty+`*

. If `+tableProperty*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TBLC'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+tableProperty*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+tableProperty_h :: tableProperty_t*+` be `+tableProperty+`*
 .. Group cons: `+TC+`, `+TBLC_0+`, and `+tableProperty_h :: tableProperty_t*+`

  ... (TableProperty_ok: `+TC TBLC' |- tableProperty_h : TBLC_1 tablePropertyIR_h+`)
  ... (TableProperties_ok: `+TC TBLC_1 |- tableProperty_t* : TBLC_2 tablePropertyIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLC_2+` and `+tablePropertyIR_h :: tablePropertyIR_t*+`

relation Table_ok: `+TC+` and `+tableProperty+`*

. Group : `+TC+` and `+tableProperty+`*

 .. Check that `+$count_table_keys(tableProperty*)+` is less than or equal to 1
 .. Check that `+$count_table_actions(tableProperty*)+` is equal to 1
 .. Let `+TBLC_0+` be `+$empty_tableContext+`
 .. (TableProperties_ok: `+TC TBLC_0 |- tableProperty* : TBLC_1 tablePropertyIR*+`)
 .. Result in `+TBLC_1+` and `+tablePropertyIR*+`

relation TableType_ok: `+TC_0+`, `+TBLC+`, and `+name+`

. Group : `+TC_0+`, `+TBLC+`, and `+name+`

 .. Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
 .. Let `+tid_enum+` be `+"action_list(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"+`
 .. Let `+(prefixedNameIR_action, _*, and _)*+` be `+TBLC.ACTIONS+`
 .. Let `+id_enum_field*+` be the list of `+id_enum_field+`, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let `+id_enum_field+` be `+$flatten_prefixedNameIR(prefixedNameIR_action)+`
 .. for each `+prefixedNameIR_action+` in `+prefixedNameIR_action*+`
 .. Let `+typeIR_table_enum+` be `+TABLE_ENUM tid_enum { id_enum_field* }+`
 .. Let `+value_enum_field*+` be the list of `+value_enum_field+`, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let `+value_enum_field+` be `+TABLE_ENUM tid_enum . id_enum_field+`
 .. for each `+id_enum_field+` in `+id_enum_field*+`
 .. Let `+varTypeIR_enum_field*+` be the list of `+varTypeIR_enum_field+`, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let `+varTypeIR_enum_field+` be `+typeIR_table_enum LCTK ?(value_enum_field)+`
 .. for each `+value_enum_field+` in `+value_enum_field*+`
 .. Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_vars(BLOCK, TC_0, tid_enum ++ "." ++ id_enum_field*, varTypeIR_enum_field*)+`
 .. Let `+tid_struct+` be `+"apply_result(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"+`
 .. Let `+typeIR_table_struct+` be `+TABLE_STRUCT tid_struct { [BOOL "hit" ;, BOOL "miss" ;, and typeIR_table_enum "action_run" ;] }+`
 .. Let `+typeIR_table+` be `+TABLE nameIR # typeIR_table_struct+`
 .. Result in `+TC_1+` and `+typeIR_table+`

relation ControlLocalDecl_ok: `+TC_0+` and `+controlLocalDeclaration+`

. If `+controlLocalDeclaration+` has type `+constantDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+constantDeclaration+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+constantDeclaration+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+constantDeclaration+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+constantDeclarationIR+`
  ... Let `+constantDeclarationIR+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+constantDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+controlLocalDeclaration+` has type `+instantiation+`
 .. Let `+instantiation+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`
 .. Group instantiation: `+TC_0+` and `+instantiation+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+instantiation+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+instantiationIR+`
  ... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+instantiationIR+`

. Else if `+controlLocalDeclaration+` has type `+variableDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList type name initializerOpt ;+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`
 .. Group variableDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+annotationList type name initializerOpt ;+`

  ... If `+initializerOpt+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
   .... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(BLOCK, TC_0)+`](Type_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(BLOCK, TC_0, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())+`
    ..... Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+variableDeclarationIR+`
  ... If `+initializerOpt+` has type `+initializer+`
   .... Let `+= expression_init+` be `+initializerOpt+`
   .... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
   .... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(BLOCK, TC_0)+`](Type_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_init+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_init+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_init, typeIR)+`
    ..... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
    ..... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_init_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(BLOCK, TC_0, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())+`
    ..... Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR nameIR ?(= typedExpressionIR_init_cast) ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+variableDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+controlLocalDeclaration+` has type `+actionDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+actionDeclaration+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`
 .. Group actionDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+actionDeclaration+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+actionDeclaration+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+actionDeclarationIR+`
  ... Let `+actionDeclarationIR+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+actionDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+controlLocalDeclaration+` has type `+tableDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`
 .. Group tableDeclaration: `+TC_0+` and `+annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+TABLE_APPLY_METHOD+`]
  ... Let `+tableProperty*+` be `+$flatten_tablePropertyList(tablePropertyList)+`
  ... (Table_ok: `+TC_1 |- tableProperty* : TBLC tablePropertyIR*+`)
  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
  ... (TableType_ok: `+TC_1 TBLC |- name : TC_2 typeIR_table+`)
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_var(BLOCK, TC_2, nameIR, typeIR_table DYN ?())+`
  ... Let `+tableDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList TABLE typeIR_table nameIR { tablePropertyIR* }+`
  ... Result in `+TC_3+` and `+tableDeclarationIR+`

relation ControlLocalDecls_ok: `+TC'+` and `+controlLocalDeclaration+`*

. If `+controlLocalDeclaration*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+TC+` and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TC'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+controlLocalDeclaration*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+controlLocalDeclaration_h :: controlLocalDeclaration_t*+` be `+controlLocalDeclaration+`*
 .. Group cons: `+TC_0+` and `+controlLocalDeclaration_h :: controlLocalDeclaration_t*+`

  ... (ControlLocalDecl_ok: `+TC' |- controlLocalDeclaration_h : TC_1 controlLocalDeclarationIR_h+`)
  ... (ControlLocalDecls_ok: `+TC_1 |- controlLocalDeclaration_t* : TC_2 controlLocalDeclarationIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+TC_2+` and `+controlLocalDeclarationIR_h :: controlLocalDeclarationIR_t*+`

relation Decl_ok: `+p'+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+declaration+`

. If `+declaration+` has type `+constantDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList CONST type name = expression_value ;+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList CONST type name = expression_value ;+`

  ... Let `+typeIR+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+type+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... If [`+typeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p', TC_0)+`](Type_wf), then
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_value+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_value+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
   .... Check that `+<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR_value>>+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_value, typeIR)+`
   .... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_value_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
   .... Let `+value+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_value_cast+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
   .... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(p', TC_0, nameIR, typeIR LCTK ?(value))+`
   .... Let `+constantDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;+`
   .... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+constantDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+instantiation+`
 .. Let `+instantiation+` be `+declaration+`
 .. If `+instantiation+` matches pattern `+%  % ( % ) % ;+`
  ... Let `+annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;+` be `+instantiation+`
  ... Group instantiation-non-objectInitializer: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;+`

   .... If `+type+` has type `+prefixedTypeName+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedTypeName+` be `+type+`
    ..... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
    ..... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- prefixedNameIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_impl* > ( # id_default* )+`)
    ..... (Inst_ok: `+p' TC_0 NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [] # tid_impl* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(p', TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_object CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_object prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?() ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+instantiationIR+`

   .... Else if `+type+` has type `+specializedType+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >+` be `+type+`
    ..... Let `+typeArgument*+` be `+$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)+`
    ..... (TypeArguments_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid_impl*+`)
    ..... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
    ..... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
    ..... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_impl* ++ tid_inserted*+`
    ..... (Inst_ok: `+p' TC_0 NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(p', TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_object CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_object prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?() ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+instantiationIR+`

 .. Else if `+instantiation+` matches pattern `+%  % ( % ) %  % ;+`
  ... Let `+annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;+` be `+instantiation+`
  ... Group instantiation-objectInitializer: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;+`

   .... If `+type+` has type `+prefixedTypeName+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedTypeName+` be `+type+`
    ..... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
    ..... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- prefixedNameIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_impl* > ( # id_default* )+`)
    ..... (Inst_ok: `+p' TC_0 NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [] # tid_impl* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
    ..... Check that `+$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR_object>>)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR_object+` has type `+specializedTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR < tid_expl* , tid'* > < typeIR_arg* >+` be `+typeIR_object+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+externObjectTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+EXTERN tid_extern rdenv_extern+` be `+typeIR+`
    ..... Check that `+tid'+`* is equal to `+tid_impl+`*
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(LOCAL, TC_0, "this", typeIR_object CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+objectDeclaration*+` be `+$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)+`
    ..... (Decls_object_ok: `+p' TC_1 { [] } { [] } |- objectDeclaration* : frame_init rdenv_init objectDeclarationIR*+`)
    ..... Let `+tid*+` be `+tid_expl* ++ tid_impl*+`
    ..... Let `+theta+` be `+{ tid : typeIR_arg* }+`
    ..... Let `+rdenv_init_subst+` be `+$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv_extern, rdenv_init)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_object_init+` be `+EXTERN tid_extern rdenv_init_subst < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > < typeIR_arg* >+`
    ..... Check that `+$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR_object_init)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_var(p', TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_object_init CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_object_init prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?(= { objectDeclarationIR* }) ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_2+` and `+instantiationIR+`

   .... Else if `+type+` has type `+specializedType+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >+` be `+type+`
    ..... Let `+typeArgument*+` be `+$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)+`
    ..... (TypeArguments_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid_impl*+`)
    ..... Let `+argument*+` be `+$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)+`
    ..... Let `+argumentIR*+` be the list of `+argumentIR+`, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let `+argumentIR+` be <<Argument_ok, the result of typing `+argument+`, under cursor `+p'+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
    ..... for each `+argument+` in `+argument*+`
    ..... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: `+p' TC_0 |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
    ..... Let `+tid_infer*+` be `+tid_impl* ++ tid_inserted*+`
    ..... (Inst_ok: `+p' TC_0 NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid_infer* > ( argumentIR* # id_default* ) : typeIR_object < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR_cast* )+`)
    ..... Check that `+$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR_object>>)+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR_object+` has type `+specializedTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR < tid_expl* , tid'* > < typeIR_arg* >+` be `+typeIR_object+`
    ..... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+externObjectTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+EXTERN tid_extern rdenv_extern+` be `+typeIR+`
    ..... Check that `+tid'+`* is equal to `+tid_impl+`*
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(LOCAL, TC_0, "this", typeIR_object CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+objectDeclaration*+` be `+$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)+`
    ..... (Decls_object_ok: `+p' TC_1 { [] } { [] } |- objectDeclaration* : frame_init rdenv_init objectDeclarationIR*+`)
    ..... Let `+tid*+` be `+tid_expl* ++ tid_impl*+`
    ..... Let `+theta+` be `+{ tid : typeIR_arg* }+`
    ..... Let `+rdenv_init_subst+` be `+$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv_extern, rdenv_init)+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_object_init+` be `+EXTERN tid_extern rdenv_init_subst < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > < typeIR_arg* >+`
    ..... Check that `+$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR_object_init)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_var(p', TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_object_init CTK ?())+`
    ..... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_object_init prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR_inferred* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?(= { objectDeclarationIR* }) ;+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_2+` and `+instantiationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+functionDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group functionDeclaration: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement+`

  ... Let `+typeParameter*+` be `+$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tid_expl*+` be the list of `+tid_expl+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+tid_expl+` be `+$name(typeParameter)+`
  ... for each `+typeParameter+` in `+typeParameter*+`
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_types(LOCAL, TC_0, tid_expl*, TID tid_expl*)+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_ret+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+typeOrVoid+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_1+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid_impl*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_1+`>>
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC_1, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+TC_2+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+FUNCTION -> typeIR_ret+`]
  ... (Block_ok: `+TC_3 CONT |- blockStatement : _ f blockStatementIR+`)
  ... If `+f+` matches pattern `+RET+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
   .... Let `+functionTypeIR+` be `+FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
   .... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+functionTypeIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* >+`
   .... If [`+routineTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p', TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+TC_4+` be `+$add_routine_overload(p', TC_0, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+functionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_4+` and `+functionDeclarationIR+`
  ... If `+typeIR_ret+` is equal to `+VOID+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
   .... Let `+functionTypeIR+` be `+FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
   .... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+functionTypeIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* >+`
   .... If [`+routineTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p', TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+TC_4+` be `+$add_routine_overload(p', TC_0, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+functionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_4+` and `+functionDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+actionDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group actionDeclaration: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+ACTION+`]
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_1+`>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC_1, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... (Block_ok: `+TC_2 CONT |- blockStatement : _ _ blockStatementIR+`)
  ... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+functionTypeIR+` be `+ACTION ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
  ... If [`+functionTypeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p', TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
   .... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_routine_non_overload(p', TC_0, rid, functionTypeIR)+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
   .... Let `+actionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR+`
   .... Result in `+TC_3+` and `+actionDeclarationIR+`
. Check that `+p'+` matches pattern `+GLOBAL+`
. If `+declaration+` has type `+errorDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+ERROR { nameList }+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group errorDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+ERROR { nameList }+`

  ... Let `+name*+` be `+$flatten_nameList(nameList)+`
  ... Let `+nameIR*+` be the list of `+nameIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
  ... for each `+name+` in `+name*+`
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `+nameIR*+` are distinct>>
  ... Let `+nameIR_error*+` be the list of `+nameIR_error+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+nameIR_error+` be `+"error." ++ nameIR+`
  ... for each `+nameIR+` in `+nameIR*+`
  ... Let `+value_error*+` be the list of `+value_error+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+value_error+` be `+ERROR . nameIR+`
  ... for each `+nameIR+` in `+nameIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC_0, nameIR_error*, ERROR LCTK ?(value_error)*)+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+ERROR { nameIR* }+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+matchKindDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group matchKindDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }+`

  ... Let `+name*+` be `+$flatten_nameList(nameList)+`
  ... Let `+nameIR*+` be the list of `+nameIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
  ... for each `+name+` in `+name*+`
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `+nameIR*+` are distinct>>
  ... Let `+value_match_kind*+` be the list of `+value_match_kind+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+value_match_kind+` be `+MATCH_KIND . nameIR+`
  ... for each `+nameIR+` in `+nameIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC_0, nameIR*, MATCH_KIND LCTK ?(value_match_kind)*)+`
  ... Result in `+TC_1+` and `+MATCH_KIND { nameIR* }+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+externFunctionDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group externFunctionDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;+`

  ... Let `+typeParameter*+` be `+$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tid_expl*+` be the list of `+tid_expl+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+tid_expl+` be `+$name(typeParameter)+`
  ... for each `+typeParameter+` in `+typeParameter*+`
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_types(LOCAL, TC_0, tid_expl*, TID tid_expl*)+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_ret+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+typeOrVoid+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_1+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+TC_1+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+EXTERN_FUNCTION -> typeIR_ret+`]
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid_impl*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_2+`>>
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC_2, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+functionTypeIR+` be `+EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
  ... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+functionTypeIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* >+`
  ... If [`+routineTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
   .... Let `+TC_4+` be `+$add_routine_overload(GLOBAL, TC_0, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
   .... Let `+externFunctionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList EXTERN typeIR_ret nameIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > ( parameterIR* ) ;+`
   .... Result in `+TC_4+` and `+externFunctionDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+externObjectDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList EXTERN nonTypeName typeParameterListOpt { methodPrototypeList }+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Group externObjectDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList EXTERN nonTypeName typeParameterListOpt { methodPrototypeList }+`

  ... Let `+methodPrototype*+` be `+$flatten_methodPrototypeList(methodPrototypeList)+`
  ... Let `+(methodPrototype_constructor* and methodPrototype_method*)+` be `+$split_constructors(methodPrototype*)+`
  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[BLOCK.KIND = `+EXTERN+`]
  ... Let `+typeParameter*+` be `+$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tid_expl*+` be the list of `+tid_expl+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+tid_expl+` be `+$name(typeParameter)+`
  ... for each `+typeParameter+` in `+typeParameter*+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_types(BLOCK, TC_1, tid_expl*, TID tid_expl*)+`
  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(nonTypeName)+`
  ... (ExternMethods_ok: `+TC_2 nameIR |- methodPrototype_method* : TC_3 methodPrototypeIR_method*+`)
  ... Let `+typeIR_extern+` be `+EXTERN nameIR TC_3.BLOCK.RDENV+`
  ... Let `+typeDefIR_extern+` be `+typeIR_extern < tid_expl* , [] >+`
  ... Let `+TC_4+` be `+$add_type(GLOBAL, TC_0, nameIR, typeDefIR_extern)+`
  ... Let `+TC_5+` be `+TC_4+`[BLOCK.KIND = `+EXTERN+`]
  ... Let `+TC_6+` be `+$add_types(BLOCK, TC_5, tid_expl*, TID tid_expl*)+`
  ... (ExternConstructors_ok: `+TC_6 nameIR |- methodPrototype_constructor* : TC_7 methodPrototypeIR_constructor*+`)
  ... Let `+TC_8+` be `+TC_4+`[GLOBAL.CDENV = `+TC_7.GLOBAL.CDENV+`]
  ... Let `+externObjectDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList EXTERN nameIR < tid_expl* , [] > { methodPrototypeIR_constructor* ++ methodPrototypeIR_method* }+`
  ... Result in `+TC_8+` and `+externObjectDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+parserDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList PARSER name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { parserLocalDeclarationList parserStateList }+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Check that `+typeParameterListOpt+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
 .. Group parserDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList PARSER name ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { parserLocalDeclarationList parserStateList }+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[BLOCK.KIND = `+PARSER+`]
  ... Let `+constructorParameter*+` be `+$flatten_constructorParameterListOpt(constructorParameterListOpt)+`
  ... (ConstructorParameters_ok: `+BLOCK TC_1 |- constructorParameter* : constructorParameterIR* # tid*+`)
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+constructorParameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+constructorParameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+constructorParameterTypeIR+` be `+$constructorParameterIR(constructorParameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+constructorParameterIR+` in `+constructorParameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_parameters(BLOCK, TC_1, constructorParameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid'*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_2+`>>
  ... Check that `+tid'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_parameters(BLOCK, TC_2, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+parserLocalDeclaration*+` be `+$flatten_parserLocalDeclarationList(parserLocalDeclarationList)+`
  ... (ParserLocalDecls_ok: `+TC_3 |- parserLocalDeclaration* : TC_4 parserLocalDeclarationIR*+`)
  ... Let `+TC_5+` be `+TC_4+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+PARSER_STATE+`]
  ... Let `+parserState*+` be `+$flatten_parserStateList(parserStateList)+`
  ... (ParserStates_ok: `+TC_5 |- parserState* : parserStateIR*+`)
  ... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
  ... If [`+methodTypeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
   .... Let `+cid+` be `+$cid(name, constructorParameterListOpt)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_parser+` be `+PARSER ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_parser_spec+` be `+typeIR_parser < [] , [] > < [] >+`
   .... Let `+constructorTypeIR+` be `+CONSTRUCTOR ( constructorParameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_parser_spec+`
   .... Let `+constructorTypeDefIR+` be `+constructorTypeIR < [] , [] >+`
   .... If [`+constructorTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](ConstructorTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+TC_6+` be `+$add_constructor(TC_0, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+parserDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList PARSER nameIR < [] > ( parameterIR* ) ( constructorParameterIR* ) { parserLocalDeclarationIR* parserStateIR* }+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_6+` and `+parserDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+controlDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList CONTROL name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { controlLocalDeclarationList APPLY controlBody }+` be `+declaration+`
 .. Check that `+typeParameterListOpt+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
 .. Group controlDeclaration: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList CONTROL name ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { controlLocalDeclarationList APPLY controlBody }+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[BLOCK.KIND = `+CONTROL+`]
  ... Let `+constructorParameter*+` be `+$flatten_constructorParameterListOpt(constructorParameterListOpt)+`
  ... (ConstructorParameters_ok: `+BLOCK TC_1 |- constructorParameter* : constructorParameterIR* # tid*+`)
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+constructorParameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+constructorParameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+constructorParameterTypeIR+` be `+$constructorParameterIR(constructorParameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+constructorParameterIR+` in `+constructorParameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+$add_parameters(BLOCK, TC_1, constructorParameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid'*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_2+`>>
  ... Check that `+tid'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_parameters(BLOCK, TC_2, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+controlLocalDeclaration*+` be `+$flatten_controlLocalDeclarationList(controlLocalDeclarationList)+`
  ... (ControlLocalDecls_ok: `+TC_3 |- controlLocalDeclaration* : TC_4 controlLocalDeclarationIR*+`)
  ... Let `+TC_5+` be `+TC_4+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+`]
  ... (Block_ok: `+TC_5 CONT |- controlBody : _ _ controlBodyIR+`)
  ... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
  ... If [`+methodTypeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
   .... Let `+cid+` be `+$cid(name, constructorParameterListOpt)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_control+` be `+CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_control_spec+` be `+typeIR_control < [] , [] > < [] >+`
   .... Let `+constructorTypeIR+` be `+CONSTRUCTOR ( constructorParameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_control_spec+`
   .... Let `+constructorTypeDefIR+` be `+constructorTypeIR < [] , [] >+`
   .... If [`+constructorTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](ConstructorTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+TC_6+` be `+$add_constructor(TC_0, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+controlDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList CONTROL nameIR < [] > ( parameterIR* ) ( constructorParameterIR* ) { controlLocalDeclarationIR* APPLY controlBodyIR }+`
    ..... Result in `+TC_6+` and `+controlDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+declaration+` has type `+enumTypeDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+enumTypeDeclaration+` be `+declaration+`
 .. If `+enumTypeDeclaration+` matches pattern `+% ENUM % { %  % }+`
  ... Let `+annotationList ENUM name { nameList_field _ }+` be `+enumTypeDeclaration+`
  ... Group enumTypeDeclaration-non-serializable: `+GLOBAL+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+annotationList ENUM name { nameList_field _ }+`

   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
   .... Let `+name_field*+` be `+$flatten_nameList(nameList_field)+`
   .... Let `+nameIR_field*+` be the list of `+nameIR_field+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+nameIR_field+` be `+$name(name_field)+`
   .... for each `+name_field+` in `+name_field*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_enum+` be `+ENUM nameIR { nameIR_field* }+`
   .... If [`+typeIR_enum+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(GLOBAL, TC_0)+`](TypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_type(GLOBAL, TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_enum)+`
