relation Decls_ok: `+p+`, `+TC'+`, and `+declaration+`*

. If `+declaration*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TC'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+declaration*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+declaration_h :: declaration_t*+` be `+declaration+`*
 .. Group cons: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, and `+declaration_h :: declaration_t*+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR_h+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+declaration_h+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC'+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... (Decls_ok: `+p TC_1 |- declaration_t* : TC_2 declarationIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+TC_2+` and `+declarationIR_h :: declarationIR_t*+`

relation Program_ok: `+p4program+`

. Group : `+p4program+`

 .. Let `+declaration*+` be `+$flatten_p4program(p4program)+`
 .. Let `+TC_0+` be `+$empty_typingContext+`
 .. (Decls_ok: `+GLOBAL TC_0 |- declaration* : TC_1 declarationIR*+`)
 .. Result in `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR* ;+`

relation Call_convention_expr_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+direction typeIR_param _ _?+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

. If `+direction+` matches pattern `+IN+`
 .. Group in: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+IN typeIR_param _ _?+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_arg, typeIR_param)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_arg_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_arg_cast+`
. Group out-inout: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+direction typeIR_param _ _?+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

 .. If `+direction+` matches pattern `+OUT+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_arg+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`>>
  ... If [`+typeIR_param+` and `+typeIR_arg+` are the same type](Type_alpha), then
   .... If [`+typedExpressionIR_arg+` is a valid l-value, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`](Expr_lvalue_ok), then
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

 .. Else if `+direction+` matches pattern `+INOUT+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_arg+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`>>
  ... If [`+typeIR_param+` and `+typeIR_arg+` are the same type](Type_alpha), then
   .... If [`+typedExpressionIR_arg+` is a valid l-value, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`](Expr_lvalue_ok), then
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`
. If `+direction+` matches pattern `+`EMPTY+`
 .. Group empty: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+typeIR_param _ _?+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

  ... If `+actctxt+` matches pattern `+ACTION+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_arg, typeIR_param)+`
   .... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_arg_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
   .... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_arg_cast+`

  ... Else if `+actctxt+` matches pattern `+NOACTION+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_arg+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk_arg+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR_param+` and `+typeIR_arg+` are the same type](Type_alpha), then
    ..... Check that ~`+ctk_arg+` matches pattern `+DYN+`
    ..... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_arg+`

relation Call_convention_argument_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`, and `+argumentIR+`

. Check that `+argumentIR+` has type `+typedExpressionIR+`
. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be `+argumentIR+`
. Group typedExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`, and `+typedExpressionIR+`

 .. (Call_convention_expr_ok: `+p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR @ typedExpressionIR : typedExpressionIR_cast+`)
 .. Result in `+typedExpressionIR_cast+`
. If `+argumentIR+` matches pattern `+% = %+`
 .. Let `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR+` be `+argumentIR+`
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`, and `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR+`

  ... (Call_convention_expr_ok: `+p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR @ typedExpressionIR : typedExpressionIR_cast+`)
  ... Result in `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR_cast+`

. Else if `+argumentIR+` matches pattern `+% = _+`
 .. Let `+nameIR = _+` be `+argumentIR+`
 .. Group nameIR-dontcare: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`, and `+nameIR = _+`

  ... Let `+direction _ _ _?+` be `+parameterTypeIR+`
  ... Check that `+direction+` matches pattern `+OUT+`
  ... Result in `+nameIR = _+`

. Else if `+argumentIR+` matches pattern `+_+`
 .. Group dontcare: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`, and `+_+`

  ... Let `+direction _ _ _?+` be `+parameterTypeIR+`
  ... Check that `+direction+` matches pattern `+OUT+`
  ... Result in `+_+`

relation Call_convention_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR+`*, and `+argumentIR+`*

. If `+parameterTypeIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Check that `+argumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+[]+`

. Else if `+parameterTypeIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+parameterTypeIR_h :: parameterTypeIR_t*+` be `+parameterTypeIR+`*
 .. Check that `+argumentIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+argumentIR_h :: argumentIR_t*+` be `+argumentIR+`*
 .. Group cons: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+actctxt+`, `+parameterTypeIR_h :: parameterTypeIR_t*+`, and `+argumentIR_h :: argumentIR_t*+`

  ... (Call_convention_argument_ok: `+p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR_h @ argumentIR_h : argumentIR_h_cast+`)
  ... (Call_convention_ok: `+p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR_t* @ argumentIR_t* : argumentIR_t_cast*+`)
  ... Result in `+argumentIR_h_cast :: argumentIR_t_cast*+`

relation RoutineTarget_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+routineTarget+`

. Group referenceExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+routineTarget+`

 .. If `+routineTarget+` has type `+prefixedNonTypeName+`
  ... Let `+prefixedNonTypeName+` be `+routineTarget+`
  ... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)+`
  ... Check that `+prefixedNameIR = ` "verify" \/ prefixedNameIR = . "verify" => p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND) \/ p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
  ... Result in `+prefixedNameIR+`
 .. If `+THIS+` is equal to `+routineTarget+`
  ... Result in `+` "this"+`
. If `+routineTarget+` has type `+memberAccessExpression+`
 .. Let `+memberAccessBase . member+` be `+routineTarget+`
 .. Group memberAccessExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+memberAccessBase . member+`

  ... If `+memberAccessBase+` has type `+prefixedTypeName+`
   .... Let `+prefixedTypeName+` be `+memberAccessBase+`
   .... Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... Result in `+TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR+`

  ... Else if `+memberAccessBase+` has type `+expression+`
   .... Let `+expression_base+` be `+memberAccessBase+`
   .... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(member)+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_base+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`

. Else if `+routineTarget+` has type `+parenthesizedExpression+`
 .. Let `+( expression )+` be `+routineTarget+`
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+( expression )+`

  ... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Result in `+( routineTargetIR )+`

relation RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue+`

. Group : `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+lvalue+`

 .. Let `+expression+` be `+$lvalue(lvalue)+`
 .. Let `+routineTargetIR+` be <<RoutineTarget_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
 .. Result in `+routineTargetIR+`

relation RoutineType_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+routineTargetIR''+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, and `+argumentIR''+`*

. Check that `+routineTargetIR''+` has type `+prefixedNameIR+`
. Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+routineTargetIR''+`
. Group referenceExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+prefixedNameIR+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, and `+argumentIR+`*

 .. Let `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)?+` be `+$find_routine_overloaded(p, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR''*)+`
 .. Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
 .. Let `+?((rid, routineTypeDefIR, and id_default*))+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+`?
 .. Let `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+` be `+$specialize_routineTypeDef(routineTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR*)+`
 .. Check that `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+` has type `+(functionTypeIR, tid*)+`
 .. Let `+(functionTypeIR and tid_impl*)+` be `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+`
 .. Let `+bound+` be `+$union_set<tid>($bound(p, TC), { tid_impl* })+`
 .. If [`+functionTypeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+bound+`](RoutineType_wf), then
  ... Result in `+functionTypeIR+`, `+tid_impl*+`, and `+id_default*+`
. If `+routineTargetIR''+` matches pattern `+% . %+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+` be `+routineTargetIR''+`
 .. If `+typeArgumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... If `+argumentIR''*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-minmax-SizeIn-BitsBytes: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", and "maxSizeInBytes"]+`
    ..... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+BUILTIN_METHOD ( [] ) -> INT+`
    ..... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-isValid: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["isValid"]+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
    ..... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+headerTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+HEADER _ { _* }+` be `+typeIR+`
    ..... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+BUILTIN_METHOD ( [] ) -> BOOL+`
    ..... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-union-isValid: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["isValid"]+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
    ..... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+headerUnionTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+HEADER_UNION _ { _* }+` be `+typeIR+`
    ..... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+BUILTIN_METHOD ( [] ) -> BOOL+`
    ..... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-set-ValidInvalid: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["setValid" and "setInvalid"]+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
    ..... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+headerTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+HEADER _ { _* }+` be `+typeIR+`
    ..... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+BUILTIN_METHOD ( [] ) -> VOID+`
    ..... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Else if `+argumentIR''*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
   .... Let `+[argumentIR]+` be `+argumentIR''+`*
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-stack-push-pop-front: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[argumentIR]+`

    ..... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["push_front" and "pop_front"]+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
    ..... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
    ..... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR [ _ ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+INT "count" ?()+`
    ..... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+BUILTIN_METHOD ( [parameterTypeIR] ) -> INT+`
    ..... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`
 .. Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-extern-method: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, and `+argumentIR+`*

  ... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
  ... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+externObjectTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+EXTERN _ { rid_f : routineTypeDefIR_f* }+` be `+typeIR+`
  ... Let `+id_arg?*+` be `+$ids_arguments(argumentIR''*)+`
  ... Let `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)?+` be `+$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ rid_f : routineTypeDefIR_f* }, nameIR, id_arg?*)+`
  ... Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((rid, routineTypeDefIR, and id_default*))+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+`?
  ... Let `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+` be `+$specialize_routineTypeDef(routineTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR*)+`
  ... Check that `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+` has type `+(routineTypeIR, tid*)+`
  ... Let `+(routineTypeIR and tid_impl*)+` be `+(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)+`
  ... Let `+bound+` be `+$union_set<tid>($bound(p, TC), { tid_impl* })+`
  ... If [`+routineTypeIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+bound+`](RoutineType_wf), then
   .... Result in `+routineTypeIR+`, `+tid_impl*+`, and `+id_default*+`
 .. If `+nameIR+` is equal to "apply"
  ... Check that `+typeArgumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-parser-apply-method: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . "apply"+`, `+[]+`, and `+argumentIR+`*

   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+parserObjectTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+PARSER ( parameterTypeIR* )+` be `+typeIR+`
   .... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
   .... Let `+_direction*+` be the list of `+_direction+`, `+_typeIR*+` be the list of `+_typeIR+`, `+id_param*+` be the list of `+id_param+`, and `+value_param?*+` be the list of `+value_param?+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+_ _ id_param value_param?+` be `+parameterTypeIR+`
   .... for each `+parameterTypeIR+` in `+parameterTypeIR*+`
   .... Let `+pid*+` be the list of `+pid+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+pid+` be `+id_param # value_param? =/= ?()+`
   .... for each `+id_param+` in `+id_param*+` and `+value_param?+` in `+value_param?*+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+"apply" ( pid* )+`
   .... Let `+id_arg?*+` be `+$ids_arguments(argumentIR''*)+`
   .... Let `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'?+` be `+$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ [rid : methodTypeIR] }, "apply", id_arg?*)+`
   .... Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*))+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'+`?
   .... Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+` has type `+(rid, methodTypeIR, id*)+`
   .... Let `+(rid', methodTypeIR', and id_default*)+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+`
   .... Check that `+rid'+` is equal to `+rid+`
   .... Check that `+methodTypeIR'+` is equal to `+methodTypeIR+`
   .... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+id_default*+`
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-control-apply-method: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . "apply"+`, `+[]+`, and `+argumentIR+`*

   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+controlObjectTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR* )+` be `+typeIR+`
   .... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR* )+`
   .... Let `+_direction*+` be the list of `+_direction+`, `+_typeIR*+` be the list of `+_typeIR+`, `+id_param*+` be the list of `+id_param+`, and `+value_param?*+` be the list of `+value_param?+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+_ _ id_param value_param?+` be `+parameterTypeIR+`
   .... for each `+parameterTypeIR+` in `+parameterTypeIR*+`
   .... Let `+pid*+` be the list of `+pid+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+pid+` be `+id_param # value_param? =/= ?()+`
   .... for each `+id_param+` in `+id_param*+` and `+value_param?+` in `+value_param?*+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+"apply" ( pid* )+`
   .... Let `+id_arg?*+` be `+$ids_arguments(argumentIR''*)+`
   .... Let `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'?+` be `+$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ [rid : methodTypeIR] }, "apply", id_arg?*)+`
   .... Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*))+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)'+`?
   .... Check that `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+` has type `+(rid, methodTypeIR, id*)+`
   .... Let `+(rid', methodTypeIR', and id_default*)+` be `+(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)+`
   .... Check that `+rid'+` is equal to `+rid+`
   .... Check that `+methodTypeIR'+` is equal to `+methodTypeIR+`
   .... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+id_default*+`
  ... Check that `+argumentIR''*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-table-apply-method: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+typedExpressionIR_base . "apply"+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... Check that `+typeIR+` has type `+tableObjectTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+TABLE _ # typeIR_table+` be `+typeIR+`
   .... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR_table+`
   .... Result in `+methodTypeIR+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

. Else if `+routineTargetIR''+` matches pattern `+( % )+`
 .. Let `+( routineTargetIR )+` be `+routineTargetIR''+`
 .. Group parenthesized: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+( routineTargetIR )+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, and `+argumentIR+`*

  ... (RoutineType_ok: `+p TC |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR''* ) : routineTypeIR < # tid_inserted* > ( # id_default* )+`)
  ... Result in `+routineTypeIR+`, `+tid_inserted*+`, and `+id_default*+`

relation Call_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+routineTypeIR+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, `+tid'+`*, `+argumentIR+`*, and `+id_default'+`*

. If `+routineTypeIR+` has type `+functionTypeIR+`
 .. Let `+functionTypeIR+` be `+routineTypeIR+`
 .. If `+functionTypeIR+` matches pattern `+BUILTIN_FUNCTION ( % ) -> %+`
  ... Let `+BUILTIN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+` be `+functionTypeIR+`
  ... Check that `+tid'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Group builtin-function: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+BUILTIN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, `+[]+`, `+argumentIR+`*, and `+id_default+`*

   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_non_default*+` be `+$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR*, id_default'*)+`
   .... Check that the length of `+parameterTypeIR_non_default+`* is equal to the length of `+argumentIR+`*
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned*+` be `+$align_parameters(parameterTypeIR_non_default*, argumentIR*)+`
   .... Check that `+$callable_builtin_function(p, TC)+`
   .... (Call_convention_ok: `+p TC NOACTION |- parameterTypeIR_aligned* @ argumentIR* : argumentIR_cast*+`)
   .... Result in `+typeIR_ret+`, `+typeArgumentIR*+`, and `+argumentIR_cast*+`

 .. Else if `+functionTypeIR+` matches pattern `+FUNCTION ( % ) -> %+`
  ... Let `+FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+` be `+functionTypeIR+`
  ... Group function: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, `+tid_infer+`*, `+argumentIR+`*, and `+id_default+`*

   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_non_default*+` be `+$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR*, id_default'*)+`
   .... Check that the length of `+parameterTypeIR_non_default+`* is equal to the length of `+argumentIR+`*
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned*+` be `+$align_parameters(parameterTypeIR_non_default*, argumentIR*)+`
   .... Let `+inference+` be `+$infer(tid'*, parameterTypeIR_aligned*, argumentIR*)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR?*+` be the list of `+typeIR?+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+typeIR?+` be `+$find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid')+`
   .... for each `+tid'+` in `+tid'*+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`, for each `+typeIR?+` in `+typeIR?*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_inferred*+` be the list of `+typeIR_inferred+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR_inferred)+` be `+typeIR+`?
   .... for each `+typeIR?+` in `+typeIR?*+`
   .... Let `+typeArgumentIR_inferred*+` be `+typeArgumentIR* ++ typeIR_inferred*+`
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred+` be `+$subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR_aligned)+`
   .... for each `+parameterTypeIR_aligned+` in `+parameterTypeIR_aligned*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_ret_inferred+` be `+$subst_type(inference, typeIR_ret)+`
   .... Let `+functionTypeIR_inferred+` be `+FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred* ) -> typeIR_ret_inferred+`
   .... If [`+functionTypeIR_inferred+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p, TC)+`](RoutineType_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$callable_function(p, TC)+`
    ..... (Call_convention_ok: `+p TC NOACTION |- parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred* @ argumentIR* : argumentIR_cast*+`)
    ..... Result in `+typeIR_ret_inferred+`, `+typeArgumentIR_inferred*+`, and `+argumentIR_cast*+`

 .. Else if `+functionTypeIR+` matches pattern `+EXTERN_FUNCTION ( % ) -> %+`
  ... Let `+EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+` be `+functionTypeIR+`
  ... Group externfunction: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`, `+typeArgumentIR+`*, `+tid_infer+`*, `+argumentIR+`*, and `+id_default+`*

   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_non_default*+` be `+$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR*, id_default'*)+`
   .... Check that the length of `+parameterTypeIR_non_default+`* is equal to the length of `+argumentIR+`*
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned*+` be `+$align_parameters(parameterTypeIR_non_default*, argumentIR*)+`
   .... Let `+inference+` be `+$infer(tid'*, parameterTypeIR_aligned*, argumentIR*)+`
   .... Let `+typeIR?*+` be the list of `+typeIR?+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+typeIR?+` be `+$find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid')+`
   .... for each `+tid'+` in `+tid'*+`
   .... Check that `+typeIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`, for each `+typeIR?+` in `+typeIR?*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_inferred*+` be the list of `+typeIR_inferred+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+?(typeIR_inferred)+` be `+typeIR+`?
   .... for each `+typeIR?+` in `+typeIR?*+`
   .... Let `+typeArgumentIR_inferred*+` be `+typeArgumentIR* ++ typeIR_inferred*+`
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred+`, obtained by repeating:
    ..... Let `+parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred+` be `+$subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR_aligned)+`
   .... for each `+parameterTypeIR_aligned+` in `+parameterTypeIR_aligned*+`
   .... Let `+typeIR_ret_inferred+` be `+$subst_type(inference, typeIR_ret)+`
   .... Let `+functionTypeIR_inferred+` be `+EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred* ) -> typeIR_ret_inferred+`
   .... If [`+functionTypeIR_inferred+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p, TC)+`](RoutineType_wf), then
    ..... Check that `+$callable_extern_function(p, TC)+`
    ..... (Call_convention_ok: `+p TC NOACTION |- parameterTypeIR_aligned_inferred* @ argumentIR* : argumentIR_cast*+`)
    ..... Result in `+typeIR_ret_inferred+`, `+typeArgumentIR_inferred*+`, and `+argumentIR_cast*+`

 .. Else if `+functionTypeIR+` matches pattern `+ACTION ( % )+`
  ... Let `+ACTION ( parameterTypeIR* )+` be `+functionTypeIR+`
