relation Decl_object_ok: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, `+frame+`, `+rdenv+`, and `+objectDeclaration+`

. If `+objectDeclaration+` has type `+functionDeclaration+`
 .. Let `+annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement+` be `+objectDeclaration+`
 .. Group functionDeclaration: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, `+frame+`, `+rdenv+`, and `+annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` be `+TC_0+`[BLOCK.KIND = `+EXTERN+`]
  ... Let `+TC_2+` be `+TC_1+`[BLOCK.FRAME = `+frame+`]
  ... Let `+typeParameter*+` be `+$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)+`
  ... Let `+tid_expl*+` be the list of `+tid_expl+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+tid_expl+` be `+$name(typeParameter)+`
  ... for each `+typeParameter+` in `+typeParameter*+`
  ... Let `+TC_3+` be `+$add_types(LOCAL, TC_2, tid_expl*, TID tid_expl*)+`
  ... Let `+typeIR_ret+` and `+tid*+` be <<Type_ok, the result of typing `+typeOrVoid+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_3+`,
and the set of inserted type variables>>
  ... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
  ... Let `+parameter*+` be `+$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)+`
  ... Let `+parameterIR*+` and `+tid_impl*+` be <<Parameters_ok, the result of typing `+parameter*+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC_3+`>>
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+TC_4+` be `+$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC_3, parameterTypeIR*)+`
  ... Let `+TC_5+` be `+TC_4+`[LOCAL.KIND = `+EXTERN_METHOD -> typeIR_ret+`]
  ... (Block_ok: `+TC_5 CONT |- blockStatement : _ f blockStatementIR+`)
  ... If `+f+` matches pattern `+RET+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
   .... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
   .... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+methodTypeIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* >+`
   .... If [`+routineTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p, TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+rdenv_init+` be `+$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+functionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR+`
    ..... Result in `+frame+`, `+rdenv_init+`, and `+functionDeclarationIR+`
  ... If `+typeIR_ret+` is equal to `+VOID+`
   .... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid(name, parameterList)+`
   .... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
   .... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+methodTypeIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* >+`
   .... If [`+routineTypeDefIR+` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `+$bound(p, TC_0)+`](RoutineTypeDef_wf), then
    ..... Let `+rdenv_init+` be `+$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
    ..... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
    ..... Let `+functionDeclarationIR+` be `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < tid_expl* , tid_impl* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR+`
    ..... Result in `+frame+`, `+rdenv_init+`, and `+functionDeclarationIR+`

. Else if `+objectDeclaration+` has type `+instantiation+`
 .. Let `+instantiation+` be `+objectDeclaration+`
 .. Group instantiation: `+p+`, `+TC_0+`, `+frame+`, `+rdenv+`, and `+instantiation+`

  ... Let `+TC_1+` and `+declarationIR+` be <<Decl_ok, the result of typing `+instantiation+`, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC_0+`,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+instantiationIR+`
  ... Let `+instantiationIR+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Let `+_ _ _ < _ > ( _ ) nameIR _ ;+` be `+instantiationIR+`
  ... Let `+varTypeIR'?+` be `+$find_var(p, TC_1, ` nameIR)+`
  ... Check that `+varTypeIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(varTypeIR)+` be `+varTypeIR'+`?
  ... Let `+frame_init+` be `+$update_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, nameIR, varTypeIR)+`
  ... Result in `+frame_init+`, `+rdenv+`, and `+instantiationIR+`

relation Decls_object_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+frame'+`, `+rdenv'+`, and `+objectDeclaration+`*

. If `+objectDeclaration*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+frame+`, `+rdenv+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+frame'+`, `+rdenv'+`, and `+[]+`

. Else if `+objectDeclaration*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+objectDeclaration_h :: objectDeclaration_t*+` be `+objectDeclaration+`*
 .. Group cons: `+p+`, `+TC+`, `+frame_0+`, `+rdenv_0+`, and `+objectDeclaration_h :: objectDeclaration_t*+`

  ... (Decl_object_ok: `+p TC frame' rdenv' |- objectDeclaration_h : frame_1 rdenv_1 objectDeclarationIR_h+`)
  ... (Decls_object_ok: `+p TC frame_1 rdenv_1 |- objectDeclaration_t* : frame_2 rdenv_2 objectDeclarationIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+frame_2+`, `+rdenv_2+`, and `+objectDeclarationIR_h :: objectDeclarationIR_t*+`

relation Enum_serializable_field_ok: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_enum+`, `+typeIR+`, and `+name = expression+`

. Group : `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_enum+`, `+typeIR+`, and `+name = expression+`

 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR, typeIR)+`
 .. Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
 .. Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_cast)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
 .. Check that `+<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR_cast>>+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
 .. Let `+value+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_cast+`, under cursor `+BLOCK+` and typing context `+TC_0+`>>
 .. Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
 .. Let `+typeIR_enum+` be `+ENUM nameIR_enum # typeIR { [] }+`
 .. Let `+value_enum+` be `+nameIR_enum . nameIR # value+`
 .. Let `+TC_1+` be `+$add_var(BLOCK, TC_0, nameIR, typeIR_enum LCTK ?(value_enum))+`
 .. Result in `+TC_1+`, `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR_cast+`, and `+value+`

relation Enum_serializable_fields_ok: `+TC'+`, `+nameIR_enum+`, `+typeIR+`, and `+namedExpression+`*

. If `+namedExpression*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+TC+`, `+nameIR_enum+`, `+typeIR+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TC'+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

. Else if `+namedExpression*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+namedExpression_h :: namedExpression_t*+` be `+namedExpression+`*
 .. Group cons: `+TC_0+`, `+nameIR_enum+`, `+typeIR+`, and `+namedExpression_h :: namedExpression_t*+`

  ... (Enum_serializable_field_ok: `+TC' nameIR_enum typeIR |- namedExpression_h : TC_1 namedExpressionIR_h # value_field_h+`)
  ... (Enum_serializable_fields_ok: `+TC_1 nameIR_enum typeIR |- namedExpression_t* : TC_2 namedExpressionIR_t* # value_field_t*+`)
  ... Let `+namedExpressionIR*+` be `+namedExpressionIR_h :: namedExpressionIR_t*+`
  ... Let `+value_field*+` be `+value_field_h :: value_field_t*+`
  ... Result in `+TC_2+`, `+namedExpressionIR*+`, and `+value_field*+`

relation SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+simpleKeysetExpression+`

. Check that `+simpleKeysetExpression+` has type `+expression+`
. Let `+expression+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
. Group expression-set-alpha: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+expression+`

 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
 .. Let `+typeIR''+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
 .. Check that `+typeIR''+` has type `+setTypeIR+`
 .. Let `+SET < typeIR'* >+` be `+typeIR''+`
 .. Check that `+typeIR'*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
 .. Let `+[typeIR]+` be `+typeIR'+`*
 .. If [`+typeIR+` and `+typeIR_key+` are the same type](Type_alpha), then
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR+`
. Group expression-set-subtype: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+expression+`

 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
 .. Let `+typeIR''+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
 .. Check that `+typeIR''+` has type `+setTypeIR+`
 .. Let `+SET < typeIR'* >+` be `+typeIR''+`
 .. Check that `+typeIR'*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
 .. Let `+[typeIR]+` be `+typeIR'+`*
 .. If [`+typeIR+` and `+typeIR_key+` are the same type](Type_alpha) does not hold, then
  ... If [`+typeIR+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
   .... Let `+typeIR_cast+` be `+SET < [typeIR_key] >+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_cast+` be `+( typeIR_cast ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR_cast DYN )+`
   .... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_cast+`
. Group expression-non-set: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+expression+`

 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
 .. Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
 .. Check that ~`+$is_set_typeIR(typeIR)+`
 .. If [`+typeIR+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
  ... Let `+typeIR_cast+` be `+SET < [typeIR_key] >+`
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_cast+` be `+( typeIR_cast ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR_cast DYN )+`
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_cast+`
. If `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% &&& %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l &&& expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group mask: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+expression_l &&& expression_r+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_l+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_l+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_r+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_r+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_l, typedExpressionIR_r)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_cast and typedExpressionIR_r_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR_l_cast, typedExpressionIR_r_cast, $compat_mask)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_reduced and typedExpressionIR_r_reduced))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_l_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_l_reduced, typeIR_key)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_l_coerced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_r_reduced, typeIR_key)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_r_coerced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_l_coerced &&& typedExpressionIR_r_coerced+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% .. %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l .. expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group range: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+expression_l .. expression_r+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_l+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_l+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_r+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_r+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_l, typedExpressionIR_r)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_cast and typedExpressionIR_r_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR_l_cast, typedExpressionIR_r_cast, $compat_range)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_reduced and typedExpressionIR_r_reduced))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_l_reduced+`>>
  ... Check that `+typeIR_reduced+` is equal to <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_l_reduced, typeIR_key)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_l_coerced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`?
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR'?+` be `+$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR_r_reduced, typeIR_key)+`
  ... Check that `+typedExpressionIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typedExpressionIR_r_coerced)+` be `+typedExpressionIR'+`?
  ... Result in `+typedExpressionIR_l_coerced .. typedExpressionIR_r_coerced+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+DEFAULT+`
 .. Group default: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+DEFAULT+`

  ... Result in `+DEFAULT+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+_+`
 .. Group dontcare: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`, and `+_+`

  ... Result in `+_+`

relation SelectCase_keyset_ok: `+TC+`, `+typeIR'''+`*, and `+keysetExpression+`

. Check that `+typeIR'''*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
. Let `+[typeIR_key]+` be `+typeIR'''+`*
. If `+keysetExpression+` has type `+expression+`
 .. Let `+expression+` be `+keysetExpression+`
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-expression: `+TC+`, `+[typeIR_key]+`, and `+expression+`

  ... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- expression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
  ... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`

. Else if `+keysetExpression+` has type `+tupleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Let `+tupleKeysetExpression+` be `+keysetExpression+`
 .. If `+tupleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+( % &&& % )+`
  ... Let `+( expression_l &&& expression_r )+` be `+tupleKeysetExpression+`
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-mask: `+TC+`, `+[typeIR_key]+`, and `+( expression_l &&& expression_r )+`

   .... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- expression_l &&& expression_r : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
   .... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`

 .. Else if `+tupleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+( % .. % )+`
  ... Let `+( expression_l .. expression_r )+` be `+tupleKeysetExpression+`
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-range: `+TC+`, `+[typeIR_key]+`, and `+( expression_l .. expression_r )+`

   .... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- expression_l .. expression_r : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
   .... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`
. Check that `+keysetExpression+` has type `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
. Let `+simpleKeysetExpression+` be `+keysetExpression+`
. If `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% &&& %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l &&& expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-mask: `+TC+`, `+[typeIR_key]+`, and `+expression_l &&& expression_r+`

  ... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- expression_l &&& expression_r : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
  ... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% .. %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l .. expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-range: `+TC+`, `+[typeIR_key]+`, and `+expression_l .. expression_r+`

  ... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- expression_l .. expression_r : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
  ... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`
. If `+keysetExpression+` has type `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Let `+simpleKeysetExpression+` be `+keysetExpression+`
 .. If `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+DEFAULT+`
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-default: `+TC+`, `+typeIR'+`*, and `+DEFAULT+`

   .... If `+[]+` is equal to `+typeIR'''+`*
    ..... Result in `+DEFAULT+`
   .... Let `+typeIR''*+` be `+typeIR'''+`*
   .... If `+typeIR''*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
    ..... Let `+[typeIR_key]+` be `+typeIR''+`*
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`
   .... If the length of `+typeIR''+`* is greater than 1
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC SEQ < typeIR''* > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`

 .. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+_+`
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-dontcare: `+TC+`, `+typeIR+`*, and `+_+`

   .... Let `+typeIR'*+` be `+typeIR'''+`*
   .... If `+typeIR'*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
    ..... Let `+[typeIR_key]+` be `+typeIR'+`*
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`
   .... If the length of `+typeIR'+`* is greater than 1
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC SEQ < typeIR'* > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`

. Else if `+keysetExpression+` has type `+tupleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Let `+tupleKeysetExpression+` be `+keysetExpression+`
 .. If `+tupleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+( DEFAULT )+`
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-default: `+TC+`, `+typeIR+`*, and `+( DEFAULT )+`

   .... Let `+typeIR'*+` be `+typeIR'''+`*
   .... If `+typeIR'*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
    ..... Let `+[typeIR_key]+` be `+typeIR'+`*
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`
   .... If the length of `+typeIR'+`* is greater than 1
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC SEQ < typeIR'* > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`

 .. Else if `+tupleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+( _ )+`
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-dontcare: `+TC+`, `+typeIR+`*, and `+( _ )+`

   .... Let `+typeIR'*+` be `+typeIR'''+`*
   .... If `+typeIR'*+` matches pattern `+[ _/1 ]+`
    ..... Let `+[typeIR_key]+` be `+typeIR'+`*
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR_key |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`
   .... If the length of `+typeIR'+`* is greater than 1
    ..... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC SEQ < typeIR'* > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`)
    ..... Result in `+( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )+`

 .. Else if `+tupleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+( % , % )+`
  ... Let `+( simpleKeysetExpression_h , simpleKeysetExpressionList_t )+` be `+tupleKeysetExpression+`
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-list: `+TC+`, `+typeIR_key+`*, and `+( simpleKeysetExpression_h , simpleKeysetExpressionList_t )+`

   .... Let `+simpleKeysetExpression_t*+` be `+$flatten_simpleKeysetExpressionList(simpleKeysetExpressionList_t)+`
   .... Let `+simpleKeysetExpression*+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression_h :: simpleKeysetExpression_t*+`
   .... Check that the length of `+typeIR'''+`* is equal to the length of `+simpleKeysetExpression+`*
   .... (SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC typeIR''' |- simpleKeysetExpression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR+`), for each `+simpleKeysetExpression+` in `+simpleKeysetExpression*+`, `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+` in `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR*+`, and `+typeIR'''+` in `+typeIR'''*+`
   .... Result in `+( simpleKeysetExpressionIR* )+`

relation SelectCase_ok: `+TC+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, `+typeIR_key+`*, and `+keysetExpression : name ;+`

. Group : `+TC+`, `+nameIR_state+`*, `+typeIR_key+`*, and `+keysetExpression : name ;+`

 .. (SelectCase_keyset_ok: `+TC typeIR_key* |- keysetExpression : keysetExpressionIR+`)
 .. Let `+nameIR+` be `+$name(name)+`
 .. Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+nameIR_state+`*
 .. Result in `+keysetExpressionIR : nameIR ;+`

relation TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and `+text+`), and `+simpleKeysetExpression+`

. If `+simpleKeysetExpression+` has type `+expression+`
 .. Let `+expression+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group expression: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and `+text+`), and `+expression+`

  ... If "lpm" = `+text+`
   .... Let `+matchMode+` be `+TBLC.MODE+`
   .... Check that `+matchMode+` matches pattern `+NOPRILPM %+`
   .... Let `+NOPRILPM n+` be `+matchMode+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
    ..... Let `+typeIR_set+` be `+SET < [typeIR_key] >+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_set+` be `+( typeIR_set ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR_set ctk )+`
    ..... Result in `+LPM n+` and `+typedExpressionIR_set+`

  ... Else if "lpm" =/= `+text+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
    ..... Let `+typeIR_set+` be `+SET < [typeIR_key] >+`
    ..... Let `+typedExpressionIR_set+` be `+( typeIR_set ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR_set ctk )+`
    ..... Result in `+NOLPM+` and `+typedExpressionIR_set+`
. If `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% &&& %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l &&& expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group mask: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and `+text+`), and `+expression_l &&& expression_r+`

  ... If "lpm" is equal to `+text+`
   .... Let `+matchMode+` be `+TBLC.MODE+`
   .... Check that `+matchMode+` matches pattern `+NOPRILPM %+`
   .... Let `+NOPRILPM n+` be `+matchMode+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_l+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_l+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_r+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_r+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_l, typedExpressionIR_r)+`
   .... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_cast and typedExpressionIR_r_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
   .... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR_l_cast, typedExpressionIR_r_cast, $compat_mask)+`
   .... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_reduced and typedExpressionIR_r_reduced))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'+`?
   .... Let `+typeIR_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk_r_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR_reduced+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
    ..... Check that `+ctk_r_reduced+` matches pattern `+LCTK+`
    ..... Let `+value_r+` be <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
    ..... Let `+i_r+` be `+$to_number(value_r)+`
    ..... Let `+n_prefix+` be `+$tableEntry_lpm_prefix(n W $to_bitstr(n, i_r))+`
    ..... Result in `+LPM n_prefix+` and `+typedExpressionIR_l_reduced &&& typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`
  ... If "ternary" is equal to `+text+`
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_l+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_l+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+typedExpressionIR_r+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_r+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
   .... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_l, typedExpressionIR_r)+`
   .... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_cast and typedExpressionIR_r_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
   .... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR_l_cast, typedExpressionIR_r_cast, $compat_mask)+`
   .... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_reduced and typedExpressionIR_r_reduced))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'+`?
   .... Let `+typeIR_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
   .... Let `+ctk_r_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
   .... If [`+typeIR_reduced+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
    ..... Result in `+NOLPM+` and `+typedExpressionIR_l_reduced &&& typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+DEFAULT+`
 .. Group default: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and `+text+`), and `+DEFAULT+`

  ... If "lpm" = `+text+`
   .... Let `+matchMode+` be `+TBLC.MODE+`
   .... Check that `+matchMode+` matches pattern `+NOPRILPM %+`
   .... Let `+NOPRILPM n+` be `+matchMode+`
   .... Result in `+LPM n+` and `+DEFAULT+`

  ... Else if "lpm" =/= `+text+`
   .... Check that `+text+` is not equal to "exact"
   .... Result in `+NOLPM+` and `+DEFAULT+`

. Else if `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+_+`
 .. Group dontcare: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and `+text+`), and `+_+`

  ... If "lpm" = `+text+`
   .... Let `+matchMode+` be `+TBLC.MODE+`
   .... Check that `+matchMode+` matches pattern `+NOPRILPM %+`
   .... Let `+NOPRILPM _+` be `+matchMode+`
   .... Result in `+LPM 0+` and `+_+`

  ... Else if "lpm" =/= `+text+`
   .... Check that `+text+` is not equal to "exact"
   .... Result in `+NOLPM+` and `+_+`
. If `+text+` is equal to "range"
 .. Check that `+simpleKeysetExpression+` matches pattern `+% .. %+`
 .. Let `+expression_l .. expression_r+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`
 .. Group range-range: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, (`+typeIR_key+` and "range"), and `+expression_l .. expression_r+`

  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_l+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_l+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+typedExpressionIR_r+` be <<Expr_ok, the result of typing `+expression_r+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+` and typing context `+TC+`>>
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` be `+$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR_l, typedExpressionIR_r)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_cast and typedExpressionIR_r_cast))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)+`?
  ... Let `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` be `+$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR_l_cast, typedExpressionIR_r_cast, $compat_range)+`
  ... Check that `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((typedExpressionIR_l_reduced and typedExpressionIR_r_reduced))+` be `+(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'+`?
  ... Let `+typeIR_reduced+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
  ... Let `+ctk_r_reduced+` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `+typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`>>
  ... If [`+typeIR_reduced+` can be implicitly cast to `+typeIR_key+`](Sub_impl), then
   .... Result in `+NOLPM+` and `+typedExpressionIR_l_reduced .. typedExpressionIR_r_reduced+`

relation TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, `+TBLS'+`, `+matchKey+`*, and `+simpleKeysetExpression+`*

. If `+matchKey*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Check that `+simpleKeysetExpression*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, `+TBLS+`, `+[]+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+TBLS'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+matchKey*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+matchKey_h :: matchKey_t*+` be `+matchKey+`*
 .. Check that `+simpleKeysetExpression*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+simpleKeysetExpression_h :: simpleKeysetExpression_t*+` be `+simpleKeysetExpression+`*
 .. Group cons: `+TC+`, `+TBLC+`, `+TBLS_0+`, `+matchKey_h :: matchKey_t*+`, and `+simpleKeysetExpression_h :: simpleKeysetExpression_t*+`

  ... (TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok: `+TC TBLC |- matchKey_h @ simpleKeysetExpression_h : TBLS_1 simpleKeysetExpressionIR_h+`)
  ... Let `+TBLS_2+` be `+$join_tableEntryState(TBLS', TBLS_1)+`
  ... (TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok: `+TC TBLC TBLS_2 |- matchKey_t* @ simpleKeysetExpression_t* : TBLS_3 simpleKeysetExpressionIR_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+TBLS_3+` and `+simpleKeysetExpressionIR_h :: simpleKeysetExpressionIR_t*+`

relation Expr_lvalue_ok: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+expressionIR # ( _ _ )+`

. If `+expressionIR+` has type `+prefixedNameIR+`
 .. Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+prefixedNameIR # ( _ _ )+`

  ... Let `+varTypeIR?+` be `+$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)+`
  ... Check that `+varTypeIR?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(direction _ ctk _?)+` be `+varTypeIR+`?
  ... Check that `+ctk+` matches pattern `+DYN+`
  ... If `+direction+` matches pattern `+OUT+`
   .... The relation holds

  ... Else if `+direction+` matches pattern `+INOUT+`
   .... The relation holds

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+memberAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Check that `+memberAccessBaseIR+` has type `+typedExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be `+memberAccessBaseIR+`
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-memberAccessExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR # ( _ _ )+`

  ... If [`+typedExpressionIR_base+` is a valid l-value, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`](Expr_lvalue_ok), then
   .... Let `+typeIR_base+` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `+typedExpressionIR_base+`>>
   .... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
   .... If `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
    ..... Let `+typeIR [ _ ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
    ..... If `+nameIR+` = "next"
     ...... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
      ....... The relation holds
     ...... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
      ....... The relation holds

    ..... Else if `+nameIR+` = "last"
     ...... If `+p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)+`
      ....... The relation holds
     ...... If `+p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)+`
      ....... The relation holds
   .... If ~`+$is_headerStackTypeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR_base>>)+`
    ..... The relation holds

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+indexAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index ]+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_index ] # ( _ _ )+`

  ... If [`+typedExpressionIR_base+` is a valid l-value, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`](Expr_lvalue_ok), then
   .... The relation holds

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+sliceAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi : typedExpressionIR_lo ]+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR-bitslice: `+p+`, `+TC+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi : typedExpressionIR_lo ] # ( _ _ )+`

  ... If [`+typedExpressionIR_base+` is a valid l-value, under cursor `+p+` and typing context `+TC+`](Expr_lvalue_ok), then
   .... The relation holds

relation Expr_inst: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO'+`, and `+expressionIR # _+`

. If `+expressionIR+` has type `+booleanLiteral+`
 .. Let `+booleanLiteral+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+booleanLiteral # _+`

  ... If `+booleanLiteral+` matches pattern `+TRUE+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+B true+`

  ... Else if `+booleanLiteral+` matches pattern `+FALSE+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+B false+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+numberLiteral+`
 .. Let `+numberLiteral+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+numberLiteral # _+`

  ... If `+numberLiteral+` matches pattern `+D %+`
   .... Let `+D i+` be `+numberLiteral+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+D i+`

  ... Else if `+numberLiteral+` matches pattern `+% W %+`
   .... Let `+n W i+` be `+numberLiteral+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+n W i+`

  ... Else if `+numberLiteral+` matches pattern `+% S %+`
   .... Let `+n S i+` be `+numberLiteral+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+n S i+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+stringLiteral+`
 .. Let `+" text "+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+" text " # _+`

  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+" text "+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+prefixedNameIR+`
 .. Let `+prefixedNameIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+prefixedNameIR # _+`

  ... Let `+value+` be `+$find_value_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)+`
  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+value+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+defaultExpression+`
 .. Let `+defaultExpression+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+... # _+`

  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+DEFAULT+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+unaryExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+unop typedExpressionIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+unop typedExpressionIR # _+`

  ... If `+unop+` matches pattern `+~+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+$un_bnot(value)+`

  ... Else if `+unop+` matches pattern `+!+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+$un_lnot(value)+`

  ... Else if `+unop+` matches pattern `+++`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+$un_plus(value)+`

  ... Else if `+unop+` matches pattern `+-+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+$un_minus(value)+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+binaryExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_l binop typedExpressionIR_r+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_l binop typedExpressionIR_r # _+`

  ... If `+binop+` matches pattern `+++`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_plus(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+|+|+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_satplus(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+-+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_minus(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+|-|+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_satminus(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+*+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_mul(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+/+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_div(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+%+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_mod(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+<<+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_shl(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+>>+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_shr(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+<=+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_le(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+>=+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_ge(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+<+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_lt(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+>+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_gt(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+==+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_eq(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+!=+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+B $bin_ne(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+&+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_band(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+^+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_bxor(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+|+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_bor(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `++++`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_concat(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+&&+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_land(value_l, value_r)+`

  ... Else if `+binop+` matches pattern `+||+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_l ==> STO_1 value_l+`)
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_r ==> STO_2 value_r+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+$bin_lor(value_l, value_r)+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+ternaryExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_cond ? typedExpressionIR_true : typedExpressionIR_false+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_cond ? typedExpressionIR_true : typedExpressionIR_false # _+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_cond ==> STO_1 value+`)
  ... If `+value+` is equal to `+B true+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_true ==> STO_2 value_true+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+value_true+`
  ... If `+value+` is equal to `+B false+`
   .... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_false ==> STO_2 value_false+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+value_false+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+castExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group castExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR # _+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
  ... Let `+value_cast+` be `+$cast_op(typeIR, value)+`
  ... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+value_cast+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+dataExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+dataExpressionIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Check that `+dataExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+{#}+`
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-invalid: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+{#} # _+`

  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+{#}+`
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-sequence: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+dataExpressionIR # _+`

  ... If `+dataExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+SEQ { % }+`
   .... Let `+SEQ { typedExpressionListIR }+` be `+dataExpressionIR+`
   .... (Exprs_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO_1 value*+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+SEQ ( value* )+`

  ... Else if `+dataExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+SEQ { % , ... }+`
   .... Let `+SEQ { typedExpressionListIR , ... }+` be `+dataExpressionIR+`
   .... (Exprs_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO_1 value*+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+SEQ ( value* , ... )+`
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-record: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+dataExpressionIR # _+`

  ... If `+dataExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+RECORD { % }+`
   .... Let `+RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR* }+` be `+dataExpressionIR+`
   .... (Exprs_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR* ==> STO_1 value*+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+RECORD { value nameIR ;* }+`

  ... Else if `+dataExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+RECORD { % , ... }+`
   .... Let `+RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR* , ... }+` be `+dataExpressionIR+`
   .... (Exprs_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR* ==> STO_1 value*+`)
   .... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+RECORD { value nameIR ;* , ... }+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+errorAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+ERROR . nameIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group errorAccessExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+ERROR . nameIR # _+`

  ... Let `+nameIR_error+` be `+"error." ++ nameIR+`
  ... Let `+value_error+` be `+$find_value_inst(p, IC, ` nameIR_error)+`
  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+value_error+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+memberAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Check that `+memberAccessBaseIR+` matches pattern `+TYPE %+`
 .. Let `+TYPE prefixedNameIR+` be `+memberAccessBaseIR+`
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR # _+`

  ... Let `+typeDefIR'?+` be `+$find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)+`
  ... Check that `+typeDefIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(typeDefIR)+` be `+typeDefIR'+`?
  ... Check that `+typeDefIR+` has type `+enumTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+enumTypeIR+` be `+typeDefIR+`
  ... If `+enumTypeIR+` matches pattern `+ENUM % { % }+`
   .... Let `+ENUM tid { _* }+` be `+enumTypeIR+`
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+tid . nameIR+`

  ... Else if `+enumTypeIR+` matches pattern `+ENUM % # % { % }+`
   .... Let `+ENUM tid # _ { id_member = value_member ;* }+` be `+enumTypeIR+`
   .... Let `+value'?+` be `+$assoc_<nameIR, value>(nameIR, (id_member and value_member)*)+`
   .... Check that `+value'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?(value)+` be `+value'+`?
   .... Result in `+STO'+` and `+tid . nameIR # value+`
. Let `+( typeIR_base _ )+` be `+_+`
. If `+expressionIR+` has type `+memberAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+memberAccessBaseIR . text+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Check that `+memberAccessBaseIR+` has type `+typedExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base+` be `+memberAccessBaseIR+`
 .. Check that `+text+` is equal to "size"
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_base . "size" # ( typeIR_base _ )+`

  ... Let `+_ # ( typeIR _ )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_base+`
  ... Check that `+typeIR+` is equal to `+typeIR_base+`
  ... Let `+typeIR'+` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `+typeIR_base+`>>
  ... Check that `+typeIR'+` has type `+headerStackTypeIR+`
  ... Let `+_ [ n_size ]+` be `+typeIR'+`
  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+D n_size+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+sliceAccessExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi : typedExpressionIR_lo ]+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_base [ typedExpressionIR_hi : typedExpressionIR_lo ] # _+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_base ==> STO_1 value_base+`)
  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_hi ==> STO_2 value_hi+`)
  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_2 |- typedExpressionIR_lo ==> STO_3 value_lo+`)
  ... Result in `+STO_3+` and `+$bitacc_op(value_base, value_hi, value_lo)+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+callExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+callExpressionIR+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. If `+callExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+% ( % )+`
  ... Let `+prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )+` be `+callExpressionIR+`
  ... Group callExpressionIR-constructor: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # _+`

   .... Let `+(cid, constructor, id*)?+` be `+$find_constructor_inst(IC, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)+`
   .... Check that `+(cid, constructor, id*)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
   .... Let `+?((_, constructor, and id_default*))+` be `+(cid, constructor, id*)+`?
   .... (Constructor_inst: `+p IC STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id_default* ) ==> STO_1 object+`)
   .... Let `+STO_2+` be `+$add_map<oid, object>(STO_1, IC.PATH, object)+`
   .... Let `+value_ref+` be `+! IC.PATH+`
   .... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+value_ref+`

 .. Else if `+callExpressionIR+` matches pattern `+% < % > ( % )+`
  ... Let `+routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* )+` be `+callExpressionIR+`
  ... If `+typeArgumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... Check that `+argumentIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
   .... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+routineTargetIR < [] > ( [] ) # _+`

    ..... If `+routineTargetIR+` matches pattern `+% . %+`
     ...... Let `+typedExpressionIR_base . nameIR+` be `+routineTargetIR+`
     ...... Let `+_ # ( typeIR_base _ )+` be `+typedExpressionIR_base+`
     ...... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", and "maxSizeInBytes"]+`
     ...... Result in `+STO'+` and `+$sizeof(typeIR_base, nameIR)+`

    ..... Else if `+routineTargetIR+` matches pattern `+TYPE % . %+`
     ...... Let `+TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR+` be `+routineTargetIR+`
     ...... Let `+typeDefIR'?+` be `+$find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)+`
     ...... Check that `+typeDefIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
     ...... Let `+?(typeDefIR)+` be `+typeDefIR'+`?
     ...... If `+typeDefIR+` has type `+typeIR+`
      ....... Let `+typeIR_base+` be `+typeDefIR+`
      ....... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", and "maxSizeInBytes"]+`
      ....... Result in `+STO'+` and `+$sizeof(typeIR_base, nameIR)+`

     ...... Else if `+typeDefIR+` has type `+polyTypeDefIR+`
      ....... Let `+typeIR_base < tid* , tid'* >+` be `+typeDefIR+`
      ....... Check that `+tid*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
      ....... Check that `+tid'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
      ....... Check that `+nameIR+` is in `+["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", and "maxSizeInBytes"]+`
      ....... Result in `+STO'+` and `+$sizeof(typeIR_base, nameIR)+`
  ... Let `+routineTargetIR' < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )+` be `+callExpressionIR+`
  ... If `+routineTargetIR'+` matches pattern `+( % )+`
   .... Let `+( routineTargetIR )+` be `+routineTargetIR'+`
   .... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+( routineTargetIR ) < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # expressionNoteIR+`

    ..... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # _ ==> STO_1 value+`)
    ..... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+value+`

. Else if `+expressionIR+` has type `+parenthesizedExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+( typedExpressionIR )+` be `+expressionIR+`
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+( typedExpressionIR ) # _+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
  ... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+value+`

relation Exprs_inst: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO'+`, and `+typedExpressionIR+`*

. If `+typedExpressionIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+STO'+` and `+[]+`

. Else if `+typedExpressionIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR_h :: typedExpressionIR_t*+` be `+typedExpressionIR+`*
 .. Group cons: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+typedExpressionIR_h :: typedExpressionIR_t*+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR_h ==> STO_1 value_h+`)
  ... (Exprs_inst: `+p IC STO_1 |- typedExpressionIR_t* ==> STO_2 value_t*+`)
  ... Result in `+STO_2+` and `+value_h :: value_t*+`

relation Argument_inst: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+argumentIR+`

. If `+argumentIR+` has type `+typedExpressionIR+`
 .. Let `+typedExpressionIR+` be `+argumentIR+`
 .. Group typedExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+typedExpressionIR+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_0 |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
  ... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+value+`
. If `+argumentIR+` matches pattern `+% = %+`
 .. Let `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR+` be `+argumentIR+`
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpressionIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+nameIR = typedExpressionIR+`

  ... (Expr_inst: `+p IC STO_0 |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO_1 value+`)
  ... Result in `+STO_1+` and `+value+`

relation Stmt_inst: `+p'+`, `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+statementIR+`

. If `+statementIR+` has type `+emptyStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+emptyStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group emptyStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+emptyStatementIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+emptyStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+assignmentStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+assignmentStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group assignmentStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+assignmentStatementIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+assignmentStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+callStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+callStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group callStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+callStatementIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+callStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+directApplicationStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group directApplicationStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;+`

  ... Let `+(cid, constructor, id*)?+` be `+$find_constructor_inst(IC', prefixedNameIR, [])+`
  ... Check that `+(cid, constructor, id*)?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?((_, constructor, and _*))+` be `+(cid, constructor, id*)+`?
  ... (Constructor_inst: `+p' IC' STO' |- constructor < [] > ( [] # [] ) ==> STO_1 object+`)
  ... Let `+tid_fresh+` be `+$fresh_tid+`
  ... Let `+tid+` be `+$flatten_prefixedNameIR(prefixedNameIR)+`
  ... Let `+typeIR+` be `+TID tid+`
  ... Let `+nameIR+` be `+$concat_text([tid, "_", and tid_fresh])+`
  ... Let `+oid+` be `+IC'.PATH ++ [nameIR]+`
  ... Let `+STO_2+` be `+$add_map<oid, object>(STO_1, oid, object)+`
  ... Let `+constantDeclarationIR+` be `+CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;+`
  ... Let `+routineTargetIR+` be `+` tid # ( typeIR CTK ) . "apply"+`
  ... Let `+callStatementIR+` be `+routineTargetIR < [] > ( argumentListIR ) ;+`
  ... Let `+blockStatementIR+` be `+{ [constantDeclarationIR and callStatementIR] }+`
  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+blockStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+exitStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+exitStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group exitStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+exitStatementIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+exitStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+conditionalStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+conditionalStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group conditionalStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+conditionalStatementIR+`

  ... If `+conditionalStatementIR+` matches pattern `+IF ( % ) %+`
   .... Let `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then+` be `+conditionalStatementIR+`
   .... Let `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+statementIR_then_inst+` be <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `+statementIR_then+`, under cursor `+p'+`, instantiation context `+IC'+`, and store `+STO'+`>>
   .... Result in `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then_inst+`

  ... Else if `+conditionalStatementIR+` matches pattern `+IF ( % ) % ELSE %+`
   .... Let `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then ELSE statementIR_else+` be `+conditionalStatementIR+`
   .... Let `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+statementIR_then_inst+` be <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `+statementIR_then+`, under cursor `+p'+`, instantiation context `+IC'+`, and store `+STO'+`>>
   .... Let `+IC_2+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+statementIR_else_inst+` be <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `+statementIR_else+`, under cursor `+p'+`, instantiation context `+IC_1+`, and store `+STO_1+`>>
   .... Result in `+IC_2+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+IF ( typedExpressionIR_cond ) statementIR_then_inst ELSE statementIR_else_inst+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+switchStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR }+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group switchStatementIR: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR }+`

  ... (SwitchCases_inst: `+p' IC' STO' |- switchCaseListIR ==> IC_1 STO_1 switchCaseListIR_inst+`)
  ... Result in `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR_inst }+`
. Check that `+p'+` matches pattern `+LOCAL+`
. If `+statementIR+` has type `+returnStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+returnStatementIR+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group returnStatementIR: `+LOCAL+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+returnStatementIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+returnStatementIR+`

. Else if `+statementIR+` has type `+blockStatementIR+`
 .. Let `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }+` be `+statementIR+`
 .. Group blockStatementIR: `+LOCAL+`, `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }+`

  ... (Block_inst: `+IC' STO' |- annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR } ==> IC_1 STO_1 _ { blockElementStatementListIR_inst }+`)
  ... Result in `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR_inst }+`

relation BlockElementStmt_inst: `+IC_0'+`, `+STO_0'+`, and `+blockElementStatementIR+`

. If `+blockElementStatementIR+` has type `+constantDeclarationIR+`
 .. Let `+constantDeclarationIR+` be `+blockElementStatementIR+`
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR: `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+constantDeclarationIR+`

  ... (Decl_inst: `+LOCAL IC_0' STO_0' |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC_1 STO_1 declarationIR'?+`)
  ... Check that `+declarationIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(declarationIR)+` be `+declarationIR'+`?
  ... Check that `+declarationIR+` has type `+constantDeclarationIR+`
  ... Let `+constantDeclarationIR_inst+` be `+declarationIR+`
  ... Result in `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+?(constantDeclarationIR_inst)+`

. Else if `+blockElementStatementIR+` has type `+variableDeclarationIR+`
 .. Let `+variableDeclarationIR+` be `+blockElementStatementIR+`
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR: `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+variableDeclarationIR+`

  ... Result in `+IC_0'+`, `+STO_0'+`, and `+?(variableDeclarationIR)+`

. Else if `+blockElementStatementIR+` has type `+statementIR+`
 .. Let `+statementIR+` be `+blockElementStatementIR+`
 .. Group statementIR: `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+statementIR+`

  ... Let `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+statementIR_inst+` be <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `+statementIR+`, under cursor `+LOCAL+`, instantiation context `+IC_0'+`, and store `+STO_0'+`>>
  ... Result in `+IC_1+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+?(statementIR_inst)+`

relation BlockElementStmts_inst: `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+blockElementStatementIR+`*

. If `+blockElementStatementIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+[]+`

. Else if `+blockElementStatementIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+blockElementStatementIR_h :: blockElementStatementIR_t*+` be `+blockElementStatementIR+`*
 .. Group cons: `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+blockElementStatementIR_h :: blockElementStatementIR_t*+`

  ... (BlockElementStmt_inst: `+IC' STO' |- blockElementStatementIR_h ==> IC_1 STO_1 blockElementStatementIR'?+`)
  ... Check that `+blockElementStatementIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(blockElementStatementIR_h_inst)+` be `+blockElementStatementIR'+`?
  ... (BlockElementStmts_inst: `+IC_1 STO_1 |- blockElementStatementIR_t* ==> IC_2 STO_2 blockElementStatementIR_t_inst*+`)
  ... Result in `+IC_2+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+blockElementStatementIR_h_inst :: blockElementStatementIR_t_inst*+`

relation Block_inst: `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }+`

. Group : `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }+`

 .. Let `+IC_1+` be `+$enter_inst(IC_0)+`
 .. (BlockElementStmts_inst: `+IC_1 STO_0 |- blockElementStatementListIR ==> IC_2 STO_1 blockElementStatementListIR_inst+`)
 .. Let `+IC_3+` be `+$exit_inst(IC_2)+`
 .. Result in `+IC_2+`, `+STO_1+`, and `+annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR_inst }+`

relation Bind_method: `+rdenv_0+` and `+methodPrototypeIR+`

. If `+methodPrototypeIR+` matches pattern `+%  % ;+`
 .. Let `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterIR* ) ;+` be `+methodPrototypeIR+`
 .. Group non-abstract: `+rdenv_0+` and `+annotationList typeIR_ret nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterIR* ) ;+`

  ... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterIR*)+`
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
  ... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+methodTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred >+`
  ... Let `+rdenv_1+` be `+$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv_0, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
  ... Result in `+rdenv_1+`

. Else if `+methodPrototypeIR+` matches pattern `+% ABSTRACT % ;+`
 .. Let `+annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR_ret nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterIR* ) ;+` be `+methodPrototypeIR+`
 .. Group abstract: `+rdenv_0+` and `+annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR_ret nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterIR* ) ;+`

  ... Let `+rid+` be `+$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterIR*)+`
  ... Let `+parameterTypeIR*+` be the list of `+parameterTypeIR+`, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let `+parameterTypeIR+` be `+$parameterIR(parameterIR)+`
  ... for each `+parameterIR+` in `+parameterIR*+`
  ... Let `+methodTypeIR+` be `+EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR_ret+`
  ... Let `+routineTypeDefIR+` be `+methodTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR_inferred >+`
  ... Let `+rdenv_1+` be `+$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv_0, rid, routineTypeDefIR)+`
  ... Result in `+rdenv_1+`

relation Bind_methods: `+rdenv'+` and `+methodPrototypeIR+`*

. If `+methodPrototypeIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+rdenv+` and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+rdenv'+`

. Else if `+methodPrototypeIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+methodPrototypeIR_h :: methodPrototypeIR_t*+` be `+methodPrototypeIR+`*
 .. Group cons: `+rdenv_0+` and `+methodPrototypeIR_h :: methodPrototypeIR_t*+`

  ... (Bind_method: `+rdenv' |- methodPrototypeIR_h ==> rdenv_1+`)
  ... (Bind_methods: `+rdenv_1 |- methodPrototypeIR_t* ==> rdenv_2+`)
  ... Result in `+rdenv_2+`

relation Bind_constructor: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+typeParameterListIR+`, `+methodPrototypeListIR+`, and `+methodPrototypeIR+`

. Check that `+methodPrototypeIR+` matches pattern `+%  % < , % > ( % ) ;+`
. Let `+annotationList nameIR < , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterListIR ) ;+` be `+methodPrototypeIR+`
. Group constructor: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+typeParameterListIR+`, `+methodPrototypeListIR+`, and `+annotationList nameIR < , typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterListIR ) ;+`

 .. Let `+cid+` be `+$cid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)+`
 .. Let `+constructor+` be `+EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR_inferred > ( parameterListIR ) { methodPrototypeListIR }+`
 .. Let `+IC_1+` be `+$add_constructor_inst(p, IC_0, cid, constructor)+`
 .. Result in `+IC_1+`

relation Bind_constructors: `+p+`, `+IC'+`, `+typeParameterListIR+`, `+methodPrototypeListIR+`, and `+methodPrototypeIR+`*

. If `+methodPrototypeIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+typeParameterListIR+`, `+methodPrototypeListIR+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`

. Else if `+methodPrototypeIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+methodPrototypeIR_h :: methodPrototypeIR_t*+` be `+methodPrototypeIR+`*
 .. Group cons: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+typeParameterListIR+`, `+methodPrototypeListIR+`, and `+methodPrototypeIR_h :: methodPrototypeIR_t*+`

  ... (Bind_constructor: `+p IC' typeParameterListIR methodPrototypeListIR |- methodPrototypeIR_h ==> IC_1+`)
  ... (Bind_constructors: `+p IC_1 typeParameterListIR methodPrototypeListIR |- methodPrototypeIR_t* ==> IC_2+`)
