relation Decls_inst: `+p+`, `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+declarationIR+`*

. If `+declarationIR*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Group nil: `+p+`, `+IC+`, `+STO+`, and `+[]+`

  ... Result in `+IC'+`, `+STO'+`, and `+[]+`

. Else if `+declarationIR*+` matches pattern `+_ :: _+`
 .. Let `+declarationIR_h :: declarationIR_t*+` be `+declarationIR+`*
 .. Group cons-none: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+declarationIR_h :: declarationIR_t*+`

  ... (Decl_inst: `+p IC' STO' |- declarationIR_h ==> IC_1 STO_1 declarationIR'?+`)
  ... Check that `+declarationIR'?+` matches pattern `+()+`
  ... (Decls_inst: `+p IC_1 STO_1 |- declarationIR_t* ==> IC_2 STO_2 declarationIR_t_inst*+`)
  ... Result in `+IC_2+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+declarationIR_t_inst*+`
 .. Group cons-some: `+p+`, `+IC_0+`, `+STO_0+`, and `+declarationIR_h :: declarationIR_t*+`

  ... (Decl_inst: `+p IC' STO' |- declarationIR_h ==> IC_1 STO_1 declarationIR'?+`)
  ... Check that `+declarationIR'?+` matches pattern `+(_)+`
  ... Let `+?(declarationIR_h_inst)+` be `+declarationIR'+`?
  ... (Decls_inst: `+p IC_1 STO_1 |- declarationIR_t* ==> IC_2 STO_2 declarationIR_t_inst*+`)
  ... Result in `+IC_2+`, `+STO_2+`, and `+declarationIR_h_inst :: declarationIR_t_inst*+`

relation Program_inst: `+p4program+`

. Group : `+p4program+`

 .. (Program_ok: `+|- p4program : _ declarationIR* ;+`)
 .. Let `+IC_0+` be `+$empty_instantiationContext+`
 .. Let `+STO_0+` be `+$empty_store+`
 .. (Decls_inst: `+GLOBAL IC_0 STO_0 |- declarationIR* ==> IC_1 STO_1 declarationIR'*+`)
 .. Check that `+declarationIR'*+` matches pattern `+[]+`
 .. Result in `+IC_1.GLOBAL.CENV+`, `+IC_1.GLOBAL.TDENV+`, `+IC_1.GLOBAL.RENV+`, `+IC_1.GLOBAL.VENV+`, and `+STO_1+`

relation Bind_arg: `+p_caller+`, `+IC_caller+`, `+p_callee+`, `+IC_callee_0+`, `+STO_0+`, `+id+`, and `+argumentIR+`

. Group : `+p_caller+`, `+IC_caller+`, `+p_callee+`, `+IC_callee_0+`, `+STO_0+`, `+id+`, and `+argumentIR+`

 .. Let `+IC_caller_inner+` be `+$enter_path(IC_caller, id)+`
